BECHDR|item=bec-canonical|file=sims/bec-canonical/PREDICTION-BEC-CANONICAL.hbp|date=2026-11-09|seat=cloud|base_commit=ac5b1580c4ad50ed2bc54e0762d1bb57f6ddee83 (aether main ac5b158)|engine_code_written=0|engine_runs=0|committed=0|frozen_before_measurement=1|lanes=EXACT (fixed rational q), SCALING (the two limits), ENGINE (two exact engines and the interval mode)|judges=judge-math, judge-design|owner_question=the canonical ideal Bose gas in an isotropic 3D harmonic trap as an exact benchmark: condensate fraction, its fluctuations and the two limits, frozen before any engine exists|owner_spec=approved in three messages and binding: model, condensate, two constructions, fluctuations, two limits, leading correction, separate observables, boundary controls, sequence|sequence=this file is frozen only after the helium-film freeze (rule SEQUENCE)|toolchain=Rust 1.81.0 (engine A), Python 3.13.16 stdlib (engine B and the reader)|fix_pass=2026-11-09: the final critic's FIX_FIRST verdict (5 blocking items, 16 fixes) and the multi-modular engine B, listed item by item in CHANGES.txt beside this file; a second pass the same day applied verifier round 1's 2 blocking and 19 minor findings (CHANGES.txt, SECOND PASS); still no engine code and no engine run|writes_external=0|json=0
BECDEF|term=format|meaning=one record per line; fields split at the first = sign; values keep their spaces and never contain the bar character, so abs(x) is the absolute value; each decimal is the exact rational it spells; x +/- u means the certified interval must lie inside [x - u, x + u]; [a, b] is a closed band; a list of values with one band applies it to each|json=0
BECDEF|term=model|meaning=owner specification: ideal bosons in an isotropic 3D harmonic trap; the ground-state zero-point energy is subtracted; level e = 0, 1, 2, ... holds g_e = (e+1)(e+2)/2 states; q = exp(-beta hbar omega) = exp(-x); Z_0 = 1, Z_1(y) = 1/(1-y)^3, Z_N(q) = (1/N) sum_{k=1..N} Z_1(q^k) Z_{N-k}(q); condensate fraction f_N = <N_0>/N = (1/(N Z_N)) sum_{k=1..N} Z_{N-k}; for rational q every value is rational|json=0
BECDEF|term=construction.1|meaning=the recursion above (owner); engine A|json=0
BECDEF|term=construction.2|meaning=the excited-only distribution (owner): E_0 = 1, E_m = (1/m) sum_{k=1..m} [1/(1-q^k)^3 - 1] E_{m-k}, Z_N = sum_{m=0..N} E_m, P(N_0 = j) = E_{N-j}/Z_N; engine B; it reconstructs the whole occupation distribution|json=0
BECDEF|term=fluctuations|meaning=owner: Var(N_0) = sum_{k=1..N} (2k-1) Z_{N-k}/Z_N - (sum_{k=1..N} Z_{N-k}/Z_N)^2, an exact control against the grand-canonical prediction Var_GC = <N_0>(<N_0>+1)|json=0
BECDEF|term=notation|meaning=one notation for the whole file: q = a/b in lowest terms; x = ln(1/q); eps = (1-q)^3; c_k = b^k - a^k (integers); D_N = prod_{k<=N} c_k^3; X_N = Z_N D_N (an integer, D16); N_ex = N - N_0; S(q) = sum_{k>=1} [(1-q^k)^-3 - 1] = sum_{e>=1} g_e q^e/(1-q^e) and V(q) = sum_{e>=1} g_e q^e/(1-q^e)^2, the mean and variance of the limit law pi(m) = E_m/E(1) (lane SCALING wrote nu and kappa2); Delta1 = S - <N_ex>_N and Delta2 = V - Var_N (lane SCALING: delta_N and eta_N); G = prod_{n>=1} (1-q^n)^-(n+2) (lane SCALING: Lambda), mu1 = sum g_{n+1} q^n/(1-q^n) (h1), mu2 = mu1^2 + sum g_{n+1} q^n/(1-q^n)^2 (= h2 + mu1); R = Var_C/(<N_0>(<N_0>+1)); F = Var_C/<N_0> (Fano); t = T/T_c with t^3 = zeta(3)/(N x^3); scaling q_N = exp(-zeta(3)^(1/3)/(t N^(1/3))); Y_N = N^(1/3)(1 - t^3 - f_N); W_N = f_hi - f_lo; crit = N^(1/3) W_N; C = 3 zeta(2)/(2 zeta(3)^(2/3)); c3 = zeta(3)^(1/3)|json=0
BECDEF|term=engine.A|meaning=Rust 1.81, std only, no dependencies, its own bignum (u32 limbs); exact mode runs construction 1 over one fixed denominator D_M, M = N_max(q), and keeps every exact value as a reduced pair of big integers; interval mode runs both recursions in dyadic numbers, each an integer pair (mantissa, exponent) with a p-bit mantissa (production p = 128), under directed rounding; an in-crate SHA-256 (src/sha256.rs, checked against FIPS 180-4 vectors) hashes its own sources for the head row; it computes no pi|json=0
BECDEF|term=engine.B|meaning=Python 3.13.16, imports only sys and hashlib (stdlib; hashlib hashes its own sources for the head row, BEC-N04), Python int only, no true division and no fractions, decimal or math import (the aether integer_only gate, BEC-N05); exact mode runs construction 2 modulo 31-bit primes p, 2^30 < p < 2^31, taken downward from 2^31 - 1 and each confirmed by deterministic Miller-Rabin with bases 2, 3, 5 and 7 (valid below 3215031751); a p that divides b or any c_k with k <= M is skipped and listed, and p > 2^30 > M divides no m <= M; inverses are pow(x, p - 2, p); integers are recombined by CRT once the product of the primes exceeds twice their bound, and each reduced fraction is recovered by rational reconstruction and confirmed (D19); engine B never forms a big rational; interval mode runs construction 2 in dyadic integer pairs at p = 128 with its own directed rounding; its own series for zeta(3) (Amdeberhan-Zeilberger), pi (pi/4 = atan(1/2) + atan(1/3)), zeta(2) = pi^2/6 and exp|json=0
BECDEF|term=reader|meaning=stdlib Python tools (integer-pair rationals with their own Euclid; no fractions, decimal or math import and no true division, under the copied integer_only gate of BEC-N05): compares the engines byte for byte, evaluates the frozen closed forms by integer Horner, certifies S, V, the pole constants, the logarithms and gamma in outward-rounded dyadic intervals (2^-512), evaluates every band in rationals and writes READ-SHORT.hbp and READ-LONG.hbp|json=0
BECDEF|term=kind.CONSTANT|meaning=a certified number that no engine run can change; it certifies arithmetic|json=0
BECDEF|term=kind.MODEL_EXACT|meaning=an exact identity, closed form or theorem of the canonical model, checked on engine output|json=0
BECDEF|term=kind.MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|meaning=an asymptotic or limit statement; the coefficients are derived, the bands are estimates|json=0
BECDEF|term=kind.OBSERVABLE|meaning=an observable kept apart from the occupation: one-body coherence, or the field expectation <a_0>|json=0
BECDEF|term=kind.CONTRAST|meaning=a law that holds for another ensemble or state (grand canonical, coherent) tested on the canonical output|json=0
BECDEF|term=kind.NUMERICS|meaning=what the engines, the reader or the process must do; not a mathematical derivation|json=0
BECDEF|term=kind.FAULTS|meaning=planted faults that must be detected|json=0
BECDEF|term=tag.DERIVED|meaning=follows exactly from stated, verified inputs by an inlined derivation; the row certifies arithmetic or an exact identity of the model|json=0
BECDEF|term=tag.CONJECTURE|meaning=anything else: an asymptotic band, an extrapolated band, an engine-property claim, or a row fed by an input with verified=0|json=0
BECDEF|term=tag.OPEN|meaning=no verdict in this freeze; a proven bound must come first in a dated addendum|json=0
BECDEF|term=tag.REPORTED|meaning=a literature result with its citation (BECCITE records); no row rests on it alone|json=0
BECDEF|term=tag.MEASURED|meaning=engine outputs only; this file has none|json=0
BECDEF|term=rule.unverified|meaning=a row whose verdict uses an input with verified=0 is tagged CONJECTURE|json=0
BECDEF|term=verdict|meaning=one convention for every row: MET if every scored read and every frozen claim holds, NOT_MET if a scored read is MISS or a stated falsifier occurs, NOT_RESOLVED otherwise; a row whose frozen claim is a pattern of sub-verdicts (some designed NOT_MET) is MET when exactly that pattern occurs; NOT_MEASURED only under rule STOP|json=0
BECDEF|term=read_and_report|meaning=an item printed with its frozen value beside it and no verdict; falsifiers are evaluated on scored reads only|json=0
BECDEF|term=control.NEGATIVE|meaning=a row that can come out NOT_MET on a real outcome, or that must catch planted faults: BEC-T01 (planted a, b), BEC-T02, BEC-T11 (the critical control), BEC-O02 (PF9), BEC-N06 (PF6), BEC-F01|json=0
BECDEF|term=fixed_by_inputs|meaning=1 marks a row whose verdict is fixed once its inputs are frozen (only an arithmetic slip, an engine fault or a re-read of a source can flip it); such rows certify arithmetic and never count as negative controls; S marks a row where only the sub-reads named in it are fixed by inputs; 0 otherwise|json=0
BECDEF|term=observables.separate|meaning=owner: condensate occupation (<N_0>, f_N), its variance Var(N_0), one-body coherence (the eigenvalues lambda_e of the one-body density matrix) and the number-conserving field expectation <a_0> = 0 are separate observables; finite-N occupation is distinct from spontaneous phase-symmetry breaking|json=0
BECDEF|term=limit.fixed_q|meaning=owner: fixed rational q with N growing; temperature stays fixed in trap units (k_B T/(hbar omega) = 1/x), the fraction goes to 1, <N_ex> stays bounded, and the correction is O(1/N)|json=0
BECDEF|term=limit.scaling|meaning=owner: thermodynamic scaling at fixed t = T/T_c, q_N = exp(-zeta(3)^(1/3)/(t N^(1/3))) enclosed between rationals by certified log and exp bounds; numerator and denominator of f are evaluated at opposite endpoints, so no monotonicity is needed; precision target N^(1/3) W_N < 1/1000, a numerical precision criterion and not a claim about the asymptotic remainder|json=0
BECDEF|term=leading_correction|meaning=owner: N_ex = zeta(3) x^-3 + (3/2) zeta(2) x^-2 + O(x^-1 log(1/x)), so <N_0>/N = 1 - t^3 - C t^2 N^(-1/3) + smaller corrections, C enclosed by certified rational bounds (not the rounded 2.18); the correction is negative; an asymptotically derived candidate, not for the narrow critical region; the canonical finite-N remainder stays OPEN until certified (BEC-T07)|json=0
BECDEF|term=supersolid.observables|meaning=definitions only, not rows, fixed now so the later link has a target: with the oscillator states phi_i (energy e_i) and the zero-point-subtracted Mehler kernel K(r, r'; y) = sum_i y^(e_i) phi_i(r) phi_i(r')^*, which in 3D oscillator units is (pi (1-y^2))^(-3/2) exp(-[(1+y^2)(r^2 + r'^2) - 4 y r.r']/(2(1-y^2))), the canonical one-body density matrix is rho1(r, r') = sum_{k=1..N} P(N_0 >= k) K(r, r'; q^k) (from D3 and D10); the density is n(r) = rho1(r, r); the coherence is g1(r, r') = rho1(r, r')/sqrt(n(r) n(r')); the pair correlation g2(r, r') is the normalized two-body density of the same canonical state; its canonical formula and every certified evaluation rule are frozen in a dated addendum before any comparison (rule SUPERSOLID_LINK)|json=0
BECRULE|id=READ3|rule=as in the stripe-phase file: an interval [lo, hi] against a band [a, b] is MET inside, MISS disjoint, NOT_RESOLVED otherwise; an exact value against an exact target or band is MET or MISS; a row is NOT_MET if any scored read is MISS or a stated falsifier occurs, MET if every scored read is MET, NOT_RESOLVED otherwise; reads without data after an engine stop are NOT_MEASURED; read-and-report items carry no verdict|json=0
BECRULE|id=INTERSECT|rule=a consistency read between two certified enclosures of one true value: MET if they intersect, MISS if they are disjoint; it never reads NOT_RESOLVED; used where one enclosure is far narrower than the other (BEC-T02 iii, BEC-T03, BEC-N02, BEC-N03)|json=0
BECRULE|id=STOP|rule=an engine run killed by its wall budget (rule BUDGET), or exiting with a code other than 0 or 3, prints no verdict; it is rerun once with the same inputs; if it stops again, every read it owns above its last completed N is NOT_MEASURED and READ-LONG.hbp states the loss; nothing is decided from partial values; the reader's certified constants failing to reach their stated width leaves those reads NOT_MEASURED; engine B at N = 262144 is not run in CI, so its reads there are NOT_MEASURED unless a local run is filed|json=0
BECRULE|id=GUARD|rule=exit code 3 with a BECGUARD row (an inexact division, a Z_n <= 0, a division by zero, an interval with lo > hi, or a failed reconstruction check in engine B, check=recon: an extra-prime or integer-identity check of D19) is information, not a stop: the row that owns the check (BEC-X02 for division and positivity, BEC-N01 for interval order, BEC-X01 for reconstruction) is NOT_MET at that point and the engine's other reads there are NOT_MEASURED; for a planted run, detected means a NOT_MET of a named row or a GUARD row|json=0
BECRULE|id=BUDGET|rule=before any long run, engine A is timed at the excluded calibration points CAL (exact mode at q = 5/8, N = 128; interval mode at t = 5/7, n = 15 and n = 32), and engine B's exact mode is timed at q = 5/8, N = 128 (ns per multiply-add per prime, s per reconstruction at the measured bit size); the measured rates (ns per limb operation, ns per interval term update, engine B's rates) are filed in CALIBRATION.hbp; each long point gets a wall budget of 4 times its predicted wall time at the measured rate; a run over budget is a STOP; the p_req reruns run only at n <= 32; the two n = 64 points run in a workflow_dispatch job or locally; no receipt other than CALIBRATION.hbp contains a time or a rate|json=0
BECRULE|id=EXPOSED|rule=a point is exposed when any seat evaluated an engine quantity there (Z_N, E_m, <N_0>, Var, P, an interval bracket) before the freeze; at an exposed point every read scored against a frozen value is read-and-report, while identity reads (A against B, normalization, structure, recombination) stay scored; closed-form evaluations at row points (hand forms N <= 3, S, V, pole sums, Mellin series, bounds) are disclosed per row as prefreeze=COMPUTED and do not demote a read, but a row whose verdict they fix carries fixed_by_inputs; the ledger is BECEXPOSURE XP1 to XP8|json=0
BECRULE|id=COMPARE|rule=C1 exact reads: A's and B's canonical strings byte-identical (MET) or not (MISS); C2 canonical form: num/den with den >= 1 and gcd 1, a distribution as one denominator and N+1 numerators with joint gcd 1, so byte equality is rational equality; engine B's fractions are reduced by construction (D19), and the reader still checks gcd 1 for both engines with its own Euclid; the unreduced X_N is compared too (engine A from its scheme, engine B from CRT), to tell a reduction fault from a recursion fault; C3 interval reads: each bracket passes BEC-N02 on its own, then A's and B's brackets must intersect (rule INTERSECT); C4 the two certified q brackets intersect and each is narrower than 2^-110 relative after rounding to the working precision; C5 engine B's head row lists, per q, its prime count, the largest modulus in bits, every skipped prime and the extra prime p*, and B's run has no BECGUARD check=recon row (rule GUARD)|json=0
BECRULE|id=STREAM|rule=large exact outputs (the 3/4, N = 512 distribution is about 120 MB of text) are streamed into the reader and hashed, never stored or committed; receipts carry form=sha256 with digit counts and a 20-digit lead when len(num) + len(den) > 96|json=0
BECRULE|id=FAULTBUILD|rule=fault builds and plant flags never produce receipts: every receipt head row lists the cargo features (empty) and engine B's plant flag (none), and the reader refuses a receipt that shows a fault|json=0
BECRULE|id=INDEPENDENCE|rule=engines A and B share no bignum, rational, modular or series code and no exact algorithm: A computes exact rationals as reduced pairs of big integers with its own Rust bignum over one fixed denominator D_M; B never forms a big rational: it computes every exact quantity modulo 31-bit primes in small Python ints, recombines integers by CRT and recovers each reduced fraction by rational reconstruction (D19), as the finite YM repo's indep_verify.py does for determinants; so a fault in A's bignum, gcd or exact division cannot recur in B, and a fault in B's residues, CRT or reconstruction cannot recur in A; B and the reader both use CPython int, and this sharing is disclosed and accepted, because the reader compares B against A and a CPython fault shared by B and the reader cannot make B agree with A; aether survey at ac5b158: agents/levels/src/bignum.rs (unsigned Big with mul_u64 and divmod_u64; no big-by-big multiply, no big division, no gcd; its crate has dependencies) is not reused, and A may follow its limb layout with a provenance note; quants/head8/src/number.rs and host8/src/bridge/number.rs are IEEE binary64 semantics in integers and must not be used; search/ste-certificate/src/lib.rs is u128 only; the planned helium-film bignum must not be shared; shared design (the denominator theorem, the atanh form for ln, the interval rules) is disclosed and every division is checked; PF5 tests engine A's bignum and PF8 engine B's reconstruction|json=0
BECRULE|id=POINTS|rule=the union excluded set (BECEXCL EXCL-UNION) and the point registry (BECPOINT) are checked by script before the freeze and in CI (tools/check_points.py): no row q equals an excluded q, no row t equals an excluded t, and any later smoke at an excluded t' must avoid t' n' in {4, 8, 16, 32, 5.6, 11.2, 22.4, 44.8, 7.2, 14.4, 28.8}, the row values of t n, since the closed forms depend on x = c3/(t n) alone|json=0
BECRULE|id=SEQUENCE|rule=owner: this benchmark is frozen after the helium-film freeze; the freeze commit of this file must have as an ancestor the commit that adds sims/helium-film/PREDICTION-HELIUM-FILM.hbp and its .sha256 sidecar (checked with git merge-base --is-ancestor); the freeze commit message must name that hash; when this file was first written the helium freeze had not happened; at the second pass the aether clone's local main is still ac5b158, and its remote main (felipe/main, 2ca50e9) contains the helium freeze ee502335b270e9f47e4c9c317c9411c1eb36a4c2 (after ac5b158, ea68fc2 and 982a82d; it adds sims/helium-film/PREDICTION-HELIUM-FILM.hbp, file sha256 392b3916..., with its GNU sidecar line; 2ca50e9 adds no sidecar and leaves scripts/check-pins.sh unchanged), and the freeze commit re-checks this on main before it is made|json=0
BECRULE|id=SEPARATION|rule=owner: this benchmark is independent of the helium-film and polariton models, and the three models stay distinct; no row, value, engine, bignum or reader code is reused from sims/helium-film or from any polariton folder, and no row here is evidence about helium or polaritons|json=0
BECRULE|id=GATE_GP|rule=owner: no Gross-Pitaevskii or Bogoliubov work for this benchmark begins before the exact canonical tests pass: BEC-C01, BEC-C02, BEC-C03, BEC-X01, BEC-X02, BEC-X03, BEC-L01 and BEC-L02 must read MET in a filed READ receipt first; BEC-N06 audits the receipts for GP or Bogoliubov output|json=0
BECRULE|id=SUPERSOLID_LINK|rule=owner: the eventual supersolid link compares explicit density and correlation observables only (n(r), g1, g2 of BECDEF supersolid.observables), defined and frozen in a dated addendum before any comparison; it never compares a condensate fraction with a stripe contrast, and nothing in this file is a supersolid claim|json=0
BECPOINT|id=GX|meaning=the fixed-q exact grid, 62 points, run by both exact engines; each engine also yields every N below N_max(q)|q=2/5, 1/2, 3/4, 9/10, 99/100, 999/1000, 1/1000000|from=lane EXACT grid with q = 1/3 replaced by 2/5 (exposure XP1) and q = 3/4 added from lane SCALING (run exactly to N = 512, judge-design); lane ENGINE's N = 256 runs at 999/1000 and 1/1000000 dropped (no value row reads them)|json=0
BECPOINT|id=GX-2/5|q=2/5|N_max=256|grid_N=1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256|ladder=16, 32, 64, 128, 256 (and 17, 33 for one-step ratios)|json=0
BECPOINT|id=GX-1/2|q=1/2|N_max=256|grid_N=1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256|ladder=32, 48, 64, 96, 128, 256 (and 33, 49, 65, 97, 129)|json=0
