BECCITE|id=R5|tag=REPORTED|source=S. G. Hoggar, J. Combin. Theory B 16, 248 (1974), log-concavity of products|verified=0|note=context only; D5 inlines its own TP2 proof sketch, so BEC-X03 and BEC-L01 do not rest on it|used_by=D5 (context)|json=0
BECEXCL|id=EXCL-EXACT|points=q in {1/100000, 1/5, 3/5, 199/200} at every N|used_for=lane EXACT smoke (SMX1 to SMX5): closed forms against construction 1, both constructions, normalization, identities, log-concavity, the GC bound, monotonicity to N = 24, q -> 0 and q -> 1 coefficients, the pole form (1/5, N = 8 to 40; 3/5, N = 20 to 60), the lambda_e identity, Mellin residuals, the truncated brute force, PF1 to PF4, cost timing|json=0
BECEXCL|id=EXCL-SCALING|points=q in {1/3, 2/3, 4/5, 43/64} at every N; t in {3/5, 4/5} at every N|used_for=lane SCALING smoke: exact recursions (1/3 to N = 64, 2/3 to 128, 4/5 to 96), the one-pole rate, the Chernoff bound, near-critical truncation, the directed-rounding prototype (43/64; t = 3/5, 4/5), the Mellin calibration (exposure XP2); q = 1/3 was also lane EXACT's row q and is moved here (exposure XP1)|json=0
BECEXCL|id=EXCL-ENGINE|points=q in {2/7, 5/8, 3/1000, 47/50} at every N; t = 5/7 at every N|used_for=lane ENGINE smoke: both constructions and both integer schemes, bit lengths, timings, gcd cost, faults F1a, F1b, F2, F3, the dyadic interval enclosure (5/8), the scaling interval smoke (t = 5/7: q bracket, crit at p = 128 and p = 16, the loose bracket, recombination, Z against E); this synthesis also ran its PF5 prototype at 5/8 and 2/7; rule BUDGET calibrates at 5/8 and t = 5/7|json=0
BECEXCL|id=EXCL-JUDGE|points=q in {49/50, 1999/2000, 1/10000000, 2/9} at every N|used_for=judge-math exact recursions: q -> 1 bands (49/50, 1999/2000), q -> 0 coefficients (1/10^7), the lambda_1 gap ratio (2/9)|json=0
BECEXCL|id=EXCL-UNION|points=q in {1/100000, 1/5, 3/5, 199/200, 1/3, 2/3, 4/5, 43/64, 2/7, 5/8, 3/1000, 47/50, 49/50, 1999/2000, 1/10000000, 2/9, 1/41, 2/41, 3/41, 4/41, 5/41, 6/41, 7/41, 8/41, 9/41, 10/41, 11/41, 12/41, 13/41, 14/41, 15/41, 16/41, 17/41, 18/41, 19/41, 20/41, 21/41, 22/41, 23/41, 24/41, 25/41, 26/41, 27/41, 28/41, 29/41, 30/41, 31/41, 32/41, 33/41, 34/41, 35/41, 36/41, 37/41, 38/41, 39/41, 40/41}, 56 q in all, the last 40 from EXCL-CRITIC; t in {3/5, 4/5, 5/7}|used_for=no row uses any of these at any N; scripted check (rule POINTS) against every BECPOINT record of this file: calc/c12_check_points.py, rerun on this fixed file in the second pass, read 56 excluded q and 3 excluded t and found 0 collisions, exit 0 (output bec-fix/r2/s2_c12_rerun.txt, BECSMOKE SM11; the saved calc/c12_check_points.txt is the first synthesis's run, 16 q, kept unchanged); the constructions at these points ran in exact Fractions or integers; Decimal and floats were used for the Mellin constants, the S and V sums, the pole tails, the Chernoff sums, the Gaussian estimates and printing, all in scratch that no engine or tool runs|json=0
BECEXCL|id=EXCL-CRITIC|points=q = i/41 for i = 1 to 40, at N <= 3|used_for=the final critic evaluated the cycle-index closed forms Z_1, Z_2, Z_3 (engine quantities) there to check the D1 identities (critic/k1_closed.py); they are not row points and join EXCL-UNION; the critic's exact runs at 1/5, 3/5, 2/3, 1/100000, 1/10000000, 2/7, 47/50 and 3/1000 were already in the union (BECSMOKE SM8)|json=0
BECEXPOSURE|id=XP1|point=q = 1/3|seen=lane SCALING ran both exact constructions at q = 1/3 for N <= 64 (scaling/smoke_exact.txt, smoke_eta.txt) and printed Delta1, Var, eta and Delta1/pole at N = 1 to 64; lane EXACT had frozen values there (its rule EXPOSED said CROSS_READ: none, true only for that lane); both judges and this synthesis read the files (CROSS_READ)|handling=q = 1/3 is removed from every row and joins the excluded set; the grid uses q = 2/5, which no seat had used (checked by search of every lane and judge script); every q = 2/5 value is recomputed from closed forms only; no frozen value at 1/3 remains|json=0
BECEXPOSURE|id=XP2|point=seven row values of x = c3/(t n)|seen=lane SCALING's Mellin calibration at excluded t' evaluated the closed-form series S(e^-x) and V(e^-x) at t' n' = t n for TS (1/2; 8, 16, 32, 64), (9/10; 16, 32) and TC (9/10, 8) (scaling/mellin.py, mellin_calibration.txt; its header line saying no row t n is used is false); since <N_ex>_N = S(q_N) - Delta1 with ln Delta1 <= -84, this fixes the engine's <N_0> there to about 36 digits; it is not an engine run; later seats evaluated only Mellin forms at row t n: the final critic at every TS and TC t n (k4, SM8), the fix pass at TC (f1_gauss.py) and at t = 7/10 (f11_t710.py), SM9, and verifier round 1 (SM10) at TC, (1/2, 8), (9/10, 16) and (9/10, 32), and at (7/10, 8) for M and x(N - S) only, plus the Chernoff ln B1 at (1/2, 8)|handling=kept scored; prefreeze=COMPUTED in every row that reads those points; the scored reads there are fixed_by_inputs (S); no seat evaluated the series at the four t = 7/10 points (t n = 5.6, 11.2, 22.4, 44.8), where only Mellin forms were evaluated (final critic k4, fix-pass f11_t710.py, and verifier round 1 at (7/10, 8)), but they are not blind either: the frozen six-term Mellin values fix Y_N there to 2.4e-13 or better, g_N to 2.9e-12 or better and Var/N to 3.1e-12 (relative) or better, if the D9 residual pattern holds, at least 8 orders inside BAND_Y and 6 orders inside the sharp bands, so the BEC-T04, T06 and T08 reads at t = 7/10 test the arithmetic and the engines, not the expansion (final critic; sizes fix-pass f11_t710.py, Mellin forms only)|json=0
BECEXPOSURE|id=XP3|point=every grid point with N <= 6|seen=lane EXACT's symbolic recursion (mono_sturm.py) holds every Z_{N-k}/Z_N for N <= 6 as a rational function of q; it was evaluated numerically only at the excluded q = 1/5|handling=disclosed in each row that reads an N = 4 value (BEC-X01, BEC-L06, BEC-B02, BEC-G01, BEC-G02); no N = 4 value is frozen|json=0
BECEXPOSURE|id=XP4|point=every row q at N <= 3|seen=the hand closed forms were evaluated at row q by lane EXACT (derive_closed.py E), lane ENGINE (closed_forms.py, N <= 2), judge-math (j1_closed.py), judge-design (by hand), this synthesis (calc/c2_closed.py) and the final critic (critic/k1_closed.py: every BEC-C01 to C03 string from the cycle index; critic/k8_selfconsistency.py: the N <= 3 sub-reads of BEC-B01, B02, L01, L02, L06, X03, G01 and G02 against their frozen bands, all holding); verifier round 1 (SM10: v1_closed.py, the N <= 3 integer polynomials of both recursions, then the 110 BEC-C01 to C03 strings, the 16 boundary fingerprints, normalization and the variance identity at the seven row q; v5_multimod.py, the N = 2, 3 modulus needs read from the frozen BEC-C02 and C03 strings; v6_spot.py, the PF9 value and the fault values at q = 1/2)|handling=prefreeze=COMPUTED; BEC-C01 to BEC-C03 carry fixed_by_inputs=1; the N <= 3 sub-reads of BEC-L01, L02, L06, X01 (d), X02, X03, O01, B01, B02, G01 and G02 are fixed by those strings, so these rows carry fixed_by_inputs=S and cite XP4 (no seat evaluated the X01 (d), X02 and O01 sub-reads themselves; verifier round 1 checked normalization and the variance identity at N <= 3 from the same closed forms, v1_closed.py)|json=0
BECEXPOSURE|id=XP5|point=row points, closed forms|seen=S, V, G, mu1, mu2, C2/H(1), pole sums, fixed-q Mellin residuals, q_N, Chernoff bounds, p_req and W_bound, t_c, t_M6, t_M8, bits(D_N), t_N(q) at row points (lanes, judge-math, this synthesis); the final critic (critic/k2 constants and the 62 t_N(q) and 11 q_N; k3 the fixed-q closed forms of BEC-L02 to L05, G01, G02 and B02; k4 Mellin forms at every TS and TC t n, t = 7/10 included, and ln B at four exposed points; k6 counts; k7 the gcd-loss rule at q = 1/1000000 from b - a alone; k9 the Gaussian estimate at TC); the fix pass (bec-fix: the corrected Gaussian at TC, the D13 bound at TC and at p_req - 16, the Jensen gap sizes at TS and TC from frozen f values, the gcd-loss rule at the 29 BEC-X04 points, the third cumulant k3 and the corrected gap estimates at the BEC-L04 ladders, bits(D_N) for engine B's prime counts, the t = 7/10 residual sizes from Mellin forms); verifier round 1 (SM10: the BEC-K01 intervals, ln(5/2), ln(10^6), t_N(q) at 4 points, q_N at (1/2, 8) and (9/10, 32), the D13 bound and p_req at the 11 scaling points from the frozen f values, at the 15 BEC-L04 ladder points S, V, G, mu1, k2, k3, H(1), E(1), the pole sums Delta1, Delta2, f, Var, R, F and the gap-ratio estimates, the L02 thresholds, the G01 and G02 bounds at (2/5, 16), the B01 integers, the B02 coefficients, the L05 PF7 values, the X02 counts, bits(D_N) at 5 BEC-X04 points and at the CS points, and the per-prime gcd-loss rule at the 29 BEC-X04 points from a, b and N alone); the second pass (SM11: the same gcd-loss rule at the 29 points, the BEC-X04 bands at q = 1/1000000, N = 16, and (N^2 + 8N) u at p_req - 16)|handling=prefreeze=COMPUTED per row; reads against them certify arithmetic unless the row says otherwise|json=0
BECEXPOSURE|id=XP6|point=judge-math points|seen=exact recursions at q in {49/50, 1999/2000, 1/10^7, 2/9}|handling=those q join the excluded set (EXCL-JUDGE)|json=0
BECEXPOSURE|id=XP7|point=lane scratch read by others|seen=both judges and this synthesis read every lane scratch file; lane ENGINE read the other lanes' point lists only (CROSS_READ, no values)|handling=covered by XP1 and XP2; no other engine quantity at a row point was seen|json=0
BECEXPOSURE|id=XP8|point=unexposed|seen=no seat evaluated Z_N, E_m or any engine quantity at q = 2/5 or q = 3/4 beyond the N <= 3 closed forms of XP4 (the q = 3/4 one-pole values of lane SCALING and judge-math are closed forms), nor at any t = 7/10 scaling point (there only closed forms were evaluated: Mellin forms by the final critic k4 at all four points, by fix-pass f11_t710.py, and by verifier round 1 at (7/10, 8) for M and x(N - S) only; and the q_N enclosure by the final critic k2 and the fix pass)|handling=these points carry the blind reads of BEC-L04 and BEC-G02 (2/5, 16); at t = 7/10 no engine quantity was seen, but the BEC-T04, T06 and T08 reads there test arithmetic and the engines, not the expansion (XP2)|json=0
