BECSMOKE|id=SM8|seat=final critic|calls=scripts in bec/critic, each with a .txt output: k1_closed.py (every BEC-C01 to C03 string and the 16 boundary fingerprints from the cycle index at the seven row q, XP4; the D1 identities at q = i/41, i = 1 to 40, EXCL-CRITIC); k2_constants.py (BEC-K01 by independent series: Euler-Maclaurin zeta(3), zeta(2) and gamma, a Machin check of pi^2/6, Decimal ln and exp; the 7 logarithms, the 62 t_N(q) and the 11 q_N, XP5); k3_fixedq.py (the closed forms of BEC-L02 to L05, G01, G02 and B02 at row q, XP5); k4_scaling.py (Mellin forms at every TS and TC t n, t = 7/10 included, and ln B1, ln B2 at four exposed points, XP5); k5_excluded.py (exact recursions at the excluded 1/5, 3/5, 2/3: the gap against Delta1, always below 1/3; and at 1/100000, 1/10000000, 3/1000: bits of den Z_N); k6_counts.py (counts of GX, X02, X04, B01, TRUNC and the fault values); k7_varbits.py (exact recursions at the excluded 1/100000, 1/10000000, 2/7, 47/50: bits of den Z_N and den Var; the gcd-loss rule at the row q = 1/1000000 from b - a alone, no row value); k8_selfconsistency.py (the N <= 3 sub-reads of BEC-B01, B02, L01, L02, L06, X03, G01 and G02 from the frozen closed forms at the row q, XP4, all holding); k9_gauss.py (the truncated-Gaussian estimate in floats at TC from Mellin forms, XP2, and at the excluded (t, n) = (4/5, 6)); fingerprints (sha256, first 16 hex, script then output): k1 c3ed8d2e48706aaf, ee4c77f6a3e340ad; k2 54401db0e4996ddd, 59874d1434e9beb0; k3 966f132cb472edd8, e75d4ecd75e5ab37; k4 79a3efc2318fb817, e7f0c63fd05128e1; k5 54508e88cc80234e, be41eaf550c4aeb4; k6 1bf1a9844af32e8c, bbe0204ae168c80d; k7 5a664bafff15f173, 3549a4c018334e8d; k8 2285429c2fa96be6, ea046d21237fd78a; k9 87c6ad5c78f952e4, 61bf1db9fdaadb09|excluded=0 failures in its checks of frozen values; the gap ratio 0.118 to 0.317 at the excluded q, while the first synthesis's pole-law estimate reached 334; gcd losses of 19 bits at N = 16 at 1/100000 and 1/10000000; the exact Delta1 at (4/5, 6) about 2.2 times the corrected Gaussian estimate|json=0
BECSMOKE|id=SM9|seat=this fix pass|calls=scripts in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/b2fb539a-cb4d-5f0b-a22f-ca1a7fcb500d/scratchpad/bec-fix, each with a .txt output: f1_gauss.py (the corrected truncated-Gaussian estimate at TC from Mellin forms in 60-digit Decimal, XP2; the exact Delta1 at the excluded (t, n) = (4/5, 6) by a 60-digit Decimal recursion, and at the excluded q = 2/3, N = 32 to 56, by Fractions); f2_precision.py (the D13 bound in exact rationals at TC with the Gaussian f, the f_hi thresholds for p_req, p_req - 16, the bound and (N^2 + 8N) u at the 9 points with n <= 32, the rerun costs; XP5); f3_o01.py (the Jensen gap sizes from frozen f values and the D13 width estimates at TS and TC, Decimal; XP5); f4_x04.py (the gcd-loss sum at the 29 BEC-X04 points from b - a and N alone; exact recursions at the excluded 1/100000, 1/10000000, 43/64, 1/5, 2/9, 3/5 and 2/7 for N = 8, 16, 24); f5_gap.py with f5_gap_lib.py (the exact gap and Delta1 by Fractions at the excluded 1/5, 1/3, 2/9, 3/5 and 2/3 against the corrected estimate); f6_gap_rows.py (closed forms at the BEC-L04 ladder points: k3, the corrected gap estimates and the Delta1 pole sums; XP5); f7_mm_smoke.py (engine B's multi-modular method against Fractions at the excluded 5/8 and 2/7, the PF8 plants, and timing at 5/8); f8_badprime_search.py (prime factors in (2^30, 2^31) of c_k = b^k - a^k at the excluded 5/8, 2/7, 47/50, 3/1000, 1/5, 3/5, 2/3 and 1/3; integers only); f9_mm_cost.py (engine B's prime counts and costs from bits(D_N) at GX and the measured rates; XP5); f11_t710.py (the t = 7/10 residual sizes from Mellin forms, XP5; the FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 vectors); f10_check.py (record counts, tags, controls, required fields and the pronoun scan on this package; no .txt fingerprint, since its output reads this file); rep.py and patches/p1 to p8 (text edits only, no computation); fingerprints (sha256, first 16 hex, script then output): f1_gauss 957c5fca05a31182, f14e9b5a4cba3950; f2_precision 3fe83317671b31db, e1f5