BECRECON|id=RC1|text=independently derived by two lanes and frozen once here: S = nu and V = kappa2 (BEC-L03, 30 digits); G = Lambda, mu1 = h1, mu2 = h2 + mu1 (BEC-L04); Delta1 = delta_N and Delta2 = eta_N at q = 1/2 and 3/4 (agree to 10 digits; one-step ratios agree to the last printed digit up to rounding); the Mellin series of S and V (lane EXACT D9, lane SCALING D4, D5; D9 here); the N = 1 and N = 2 closed forms (lanes EXACT and ENGINE; BEC-C01, BEC-C02); the constants (lanes SCALING and ENGINE; BEC-K01); one interval design at production p = 128 with precision reruns replaces lane SCALING's p = 63 and p = 320 and lane ENGINE's p = 128 (judge-design); the fixed-q ladders of lane SCALING run in the exact engines; lane SCALING's 11-digit values at (3/4, 192) differ from the D4 form in the 10th digit (7.6946266073e-9 against 7.694626607854e-9 for Delta1), a 1e-10 relative difference far inside the band; the D4 form is frozen, confirmed by an independent 90-digit computation (calc/c13_pole_check.py)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-K01|kind=CONSTANT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Certified constants, from rational series with rigorous remainders and integer root bracketing; no float (D14). zeta(3) by Apery's alternating series in engine A and the reader, and by the Amdeberhan-Zeilberger series in engine B; zeta(2) = 3 sum 1/(k^2 C(2k,k)) in engine A and the reader, with no pi, and zeta(2) = pi^2/6 in engine B from its own pi (pi/4 = atan(1/2) + atan(1/3)), so the two zeta(2) brackets come from independent identities; c3 = zeta(3)^(1/3) and zeta(3)^(2/3) by integer cube roots; C = 3 zeta(2)/(2 zeta(3)^(2/3)) by outward division, the owner's C and not the rounded 2.18; gamma by the enveloping Euler-Maclaurin series (one certified gamma for every row that uses it). Elementary integral-test brackets cross-check zeta(3) and zeta(2).|points=constants (no point)|predicted=zeta(3) in [1.202056903159594285399738161511, 1.202056903159594285399738161512]; zeta(2) in [1.644934066848226436472415166646, 1.644934066848226436472415166647]; c3 in [1.063265385316368482253303125192, 1.063265385316368482253303125193]; zeta(3)^(2/3) in [1.130533279611965537269937046421, 1.130533279611965537269937046422]; C in [2.182510806863844877748836363519, 2.182510806863844877748836363520]; C - 2.18 in [0.002510806863844877748836363519, 0.002510806863844877748836363520], so 2.18 lies outside the C enclosure; zeta(2)/zeta(3) in [1.368432777620205875736765853984, 1.368432777620205875736765853985]; gamma in [0.577215664901532860606512090082, 0.577215664901532860606512090083]; gamma - 19/24 in [-0.214451001765133806060154576585, -0.214451001765133806060154576584]; C t^2 in [0.545627701715961219437209, 0.545627701715961219437210], [1.069430295363283990096929, 1.069430295363283990096930], [1.767833753559714350976557, 1.767833753559714350976558] at t = 1/2, 7/10, 9/10; (zeta(2)/zeta(3)) t^3 in [0.171054097202525734467095, 0.171054097202525734467096], [0.469372442723730615377710, 0.469372442723730615377711], [0.997587494885130083412102, 0.997587494885130083412103]; crude brackets zeta(3) in [1.202056902660, 1.202056903660] and zeta(2) in [1.644933567680, 1.644934566682] contain the sharp ones; the gamma brackets at n = 50 and n = 100 intersect; every engine and reader bracket is narrower than 1e-35 and lies inside its interval; the brackets of engine A, engine B and the reader pairwise intersect|verdict_rule=READ3 on every bracket against its interval; rule INTERSECT between seats; MET if all hold|method=bec-a consts, bec_b.py consts (zeta(2) as pi^2/6), tools/read.py consts; integer cube roots r^3 <= X < (r+1)^3 at scale 2^240|falsifier=a bracket outside its interval (MISS), wider than 1e-35, two disjoint brackets, or a sharp bracket outside its crude one (NOT_MET); a misremembered series identity, for zeta(3) or for zeta(2), shows as engine A against engine B disjoint|cost=under 1 s per engine|prefreeze=COMPUTED: closed-form series in exact rationals by lane SCALING (constants.py), lane ENGINE (constants.py, series_check.py), judge-math (j2_const.py) and this synthesis (calc/c1_constants.py, nums.py); no engine quantity; final critic k2 (SM8, XP5: independent series for zeta(3), zeta(2) and gamma, a Machin check of pi^2/6); verifier round 1 v4_certified.py (SM10: every interval of this row in exact rational intervals, both zeta(3) series, zeta(2) both ways, gamma at n = 100 and 50, the crude brackets)|from=SC-K01; BEC-E10 (constants); SK06 (gamma, now certified)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-K02|kind=CONSTANT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Certified logarithms x = ln(1/q) at the seven grid q, with the argument reduction of D14, and the reduced temperature of every fixed-q grid point, t_N(q) = zeta(3)^(1/3)/(x N^(1/3)), so t^3 = zeta(3)/(N x^3) (owner: temperature comparisons need separately certified logarithms). This places each fixed-q point relative to T_c. Fixed q with N growing drives t to 0, so the fixed-q limit is the deep condensed side of the scaling limit.|points=the seven grid q; GX (62 points)|predicted=ln(5/2) in [0.916290731874155065183527211768, 0.916290731874155065183527211769]; ln(2/1) in [0.693147180559945309417232121458, 0.693147180559945309417232121459]; ln(4/3) in [0.287682072451780927439219005993, 0.287682072451780927439219005994]; ln(10/9) in [0.105360515657826301227500980839, 0.105360515657826301227500980840]; ln(100/99) in [0.010050335853501441183548857558, 0.010050335853501441183548857559]; ln(1000/999) in [0.001000500333583533500142982254, 0.001000500333583533500142982255]; ln(1000000/1) in [13.815510557964274104107948728106, 13.815510557964274104107948728107]; t_N(q), 9 significant digits, each certified interval inside t_N (1 +/- 1e-8): q = 2/5: 1: 1.16040177, 2: 0.921011494, 3: 0.804577649, 4: 0.731007307, 8: 0.580200884, 16: 0.460505747, 32: 0.365503653, 64: 0.290100442, 128: 0.230252873, 256: 0.182751827; q = 1/2: 1: 1.53396770, 2: 1.21751097, 3: 1.06359380, 4: 0.966339097, 8: 0.766983849, 16: 0.608755485, 32: 0.483169548, 64: 0.383491925, 128: 0.304377742, 256: 0.241584774; q = 3/4: 1: 3.69597374, 2: 2.93349630, 3: 2.56264506, 4: 2.32831756, 8: 1.84798687, 16: 1.46674815, 32: 1.16415878, 64: 0.923993435, 128: 0.733374075, 192: 0.640661266, 256: 0.582079389, 384: 0.508493184, 512: 0.461996718; q = 9/10: 1: 10.0916874, 2: 8.00977757, 3: 6.99718522, 4: 6.35736467, 8: 5.04584369, 16: 4.00488879, 32: 3.17868234, 64: 2.52292184, 128: 2.00244439; q = 99/100: 1: 105.794015, 2: 83.9687656, 3: 73.