PREDICT|id=BEC-K03|kind=CONSTANT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Rational enclosure of q_N = exp(-zeta(3)^(1/3)/(t N^(1/3))) at the scaling points (owner: enclosed between rationals by certified log and exp bounds). N = n^3, so x = c3/(t n) needs no root of N. exp(-x) for 0 < x < 1 comes from consecutive alternating partial sums (engine A) or the positive series with its remainder (engine B), rounded outward to 2^-128 for the frozen values; a separately certified logarithm checks it. The engines certify q_N to an absolute width of at most 2^-130 and then round it outward to p bits, so the relative q width w is at most 2u = 2^(2-p) for every p <= 128 (the assumption of D13), about 2^-126 at p = 128.|points=TS and TC (11 points)|predicted=q_N, each +/- 1e-30: (1/2, 8) 0.766579899786589958794712300668; (1/2, 16) 0.875545486988877099765456607144; (1/2, 32) 0.935705876324861550650303696528; (1/2, 64) 0.967318911385930441869217932909; (7/10, 8) 0.827067622545209947244294847255; (7/10, 16) 0.909432582737835464256488269814; (7/10, 32) 0.953641747585452272001748842808; (7/10, 64) 0.976545824621380618189830572736; (9/10, 8) 0.862710805332540828630198328070; (9/10, 16) 0.928822267892270565491326429423; (9/10, 32) 0.963754257003449279960645886875; the reference bracket at 2^-128 is 1 ulp wide at every point; each engine's certified bracket is at most 2^-130 wide before rounding to p bits; both log checks -ln q_lo >= x_hi and -ln q_hi <= x_lo hold at all 11; engine A's and engine B's brackets intersect and each is narrower than 2^-110 relative (COMPARE C4)|verdict_rule=READ3 and rule INTERSECT; MET if all hold|method=bec-a scaling, bec_b.py scaling (q bracket printed in the head of each run); reader log check|falsifier=a bracket outside its band, wider than its bound, a failed log check, or disjoint engine brackets (NOT_MET)|cost=under 1 s|prefreeze=COMPUTED: exp and artanh series in exact rationals (lane SCALING qN.py; judge-math j6_scaling.py at three points;