PREDICT|id=BEC-C01|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=N = 1 closed form and the N = 1 boundary control. One boson sits in the ground state with probability (1-q)^3, so N_0 is Bernoulli: Z_1 = 1/(1-q)^3, <N_0> = <N_0^2> = (1-q)^3, Var(N_0) = (1-q)^3 (1 - (1-q)^3) = 3q - 12q^2 + 19q^3 - 15q^4 + 6q^5 - q^6, P(N_0 = 1) = (1-q)^3. Exact limits: <N_0> -> 1 as q -> 0 and -> 0 as q -> 1; Var -> 0 at both ends.|points=N = 1 at the seven grid q; engines A and B|predicted=(Z_1; <N_0>; Var; P0; P1), canonical strings: q = 2/5: 125/27; 27/125; 2646/15625; 98/125; 27/125. q = 1/2: 8; 1/8; 7/64; 7/8; 1/8. q = 3/4: 64; 1/64; 63/4096; 63/64; 1/64. q = 9/10: 1000; 1/1000; 999/1000000; 999/1000; 1/1000. q = 99/100: 1000000; 1/1000000; 999999/1000000000000; 999999/1000000; 1/1000000. q = 999/1000: 1000000000; 1/1000000000; 999999999/1000000000000000000; 999999999/1000000000; 1/1000000000. q = 1/1000000: 1000000000000000000/999997000002999999; 999997000002999999/1000000000000000000; 2999988000018999985000005999999/1000000000000000000000000000000000000; 2999997000001/1000000000000000000; 999997000002999999/1000000000000000000.|verdict_rule=C1 byte comparison of both engines against the frozen strings; MET if every string matches|method=both engines print canonical reduced fractions; the reader also evaluates the frozen polynomial forms by integer Horner|falsifier=any byte mismatch (MISS); planted PF4 (k = 1..N-1) gives Z_1 = 0 and a GUARD row; F1b gives Z_1 = 1/(1-q^2)^3 (64/27 at q = 1/2); F3 gives Z_1 = 1/(1-q)^2; PF1 in engine B gives Z_1 = 1/(1-q)^3 + 1: each must read NOT_MET (BEC-F01)|cost=seconds, inside the grid run|prefreeze=COMPUTED: hand closed forms at the row q (exposure XP4; lane EXACT derive_closed.py, lane ENGINE closed_forms.py, judge-math j1_closed.py, this synthesis calc/c2_closed.py; the lane literals at 1/2, 9/10, 99/100, 3/4 and 1/1000000 were copy-checked, 0 mismatches); no recursion at a row q; also the final critic (critic/k1_close