PREDICT|id=BEC-X01|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=The two independent exact constructions agree, and the occupation distribution is normalized against the other engine (owner). Engine A runs construction 1 over one fixed denominator D_M in exact big-integer rationals; engine B runs construction 2 modulo 31-bit primes and recovers integers by CRT and reduced fractions by rational reconstruction (D19); they share no bignum code and no exact algorithm. Sub-reads: (a) identical reduced fractions for Z_N, <N_0>, <N_0^2>, Var(N_0) and the distribution P(N_0 = j), j = 0..N, byte for byte (B forms <N_0> and Var from its own distribution integers, A from the survival sums), plus the unreduced X_N to tell a gcd fault from a recursion fault; (b) E_m(B) = Z_m(A) - Z_{m-1}(A) at every m, as the integer identity Y_m (D_M/D_m) = X_m - X_{m-1}; (c) the owner's normalization test sum_j P(N_0 = j) = 1, formed across engines as sum_j E_{N-j}(B)/Z_N(A) = 1 (inside B alone it holds by construction); (d) positivity: every E_m > 0 and P_j > 0, 0 < <N_0> < N and Var > 0 for 0 < q < 1. The survival identity P(N_0 >= k) = Z_{N-k}/Z_N and the mean and variance identities (D3) follow from (b) and are not scored again.|points=GX (62 points); (b) at every m <= N_max(q), 1328 values of m|predicted=0 mismatches in (a) over 62 points x 5 quantities = 310 reads and 62 X_N; (b) holds at all 1328 values of m; (c) the sum is exactly 1 at all 62; (d) holds everywhere|verdict_rule=C1 and exact integer identities; MET if every sub-read holds|method=bec-a exact --q a/b --nmax N_max(q) and bec_b.py exact for each q; tools/compare.py (rule COMPARE); sha256 per long value (rule STREAM)|falsifier=any mismatch (MISS); PF1 (engine B keeps the ground state) breaks (a), (b) and (c) at N = 1 while B's own vector still sums to 1; PF2 breaks (a) for Var; PF3 breaks (a) from N = 2; F6 (one digit flipped) gives exactly one MISS; PF8 (engine B with too few primes, or keeping a prime that divides some c_k) fails engine B's extra-prime check, prints BECGUARD check=recon and makes this row NOT_MET at that point (rule GUARD)|cost=engine B about 72 min of CPU for the grid; q = 3/4 to N = 512 alone is about 63 min on one core (about 102,135 primes; 30 min of residues, 26 min of rational reconstruction by the plain extended Euclidean algorithm, 6 min of CRT), q = 2/5 about 5 min, the others under 2 min each (rates measured at the excluded q = 5/8 by the fix pass; UNVERIFIED for the engine itself, rule BUDGET); engine A about 4 min on one core at an assumed 1 ns per limb operation (UNVERIFIED, rule BUDGET); reader under 3 min; the q run in parallel on the 4 cores|prefreeze=none at row points for the identities; COMPUTED for the cost field: engine B's prime counts and times from bits(D_N) at GX (fix-pass f9_mm_cost.py, XP5); smoke only at excluded q (BECSMOKE SM1, SM2, SM3; engine B's multi-modular method against Fractions and with PF8 at the excluded 5/8 and 2/7, SM9); XP4: the N <= 3 positivity sub-reads are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 (no seat evaluated them as such; verifier round 1 checked normalization and the variance identity there from the closed forms, v1_closed.py, SM10); the N <= 6 symbolic forms fix the N = 4 values but were never evaluated at a row q (XP3); verifier round 1 v5_multimod.py (SM10: D19 against Fractions with PF8 at the excluded 2/7 and 5/8; bits(D_N), beta and prime counts at the CS points, XP5)|from=BC-X04, BC-X05, BC-X06 (merged), BC-X07 (implied); BEC-E01, BEC-E02|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-X02|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=Denominator theorem and exact division (D16). At q = a/b, den(Z_N) divides D_N = prod c_k^3 and X_N = Z_N D_N is an integer divisible by b^(3N). Engine A's integer scheme divides exactly, by c_k^3 and by n, M(M+3)/2 divisions per q, each remainder checked. Engine B's construction does no big division: its inverses mod p exist because p divides neither b nor any c_k (checked per prime) and p > 2^30 > M (D19); its only big divisions are the checked exact divisions of the distribution step, d = X_N/g and n_j = n'_j/g (D19). The reader checks the theorem on both engines' reduced Z_N. A nonzero remainder or a Z_n <= 0 prints a GUARD row (rule GUARD), and this row owns those checks.|points=every N <= N_max(q) at the seven grid q|predicted=both divisibility tests hold at all 1328 values of N; division counts in engine A: 2/5 33152; 1/2 33152; 3/4 131840; 9/10 8384; 99/100 8384; 999/1000 560; 1/1000000 152; 0 GUARD rows in the clean runs|verdict_rule=exact integer tests; MET if all hold and no GUARD row appears|method=engines print their division counts and GUARD rows; the reader checks D_N mod den = 0 and (num (D_N/den)) mod b^(3N) = 0|falsifier=a failed test or a GUARD row (NOT_MET); F3 fails the test that b^(3N) divides X_N at N = 1 (Z_1 D_1 = b^2 (b-a)); F1b gives den(Z_1) not dividing D_1; PF4 gives GUARD positive at N = 1; PF5 is expected to give an inexact division at some n >= 2 at the first CS point, since c_1 = 1 at q = 1/2 and 3/4 makes every n = 1 division exact and k = 2 divides by c_2^3 = 27 or 343 (BEC-F01)|cost=under 1 min at the reader for the grid|prefreeze=none at row points; smoke at excluded q (SM3: both tests and both schemes, N <= 24); XP4: the N <= 3 divisibility sub-reads are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 (no seat evaluated the tests; verifier round 1 checked the N <= 3 forms as integer polynomials, symbolically, v1_closed.py); the division counts M(M+3)/2 were recounted by the final critic (k6, SM8) and verifier round 1 (v6_spot.py, SM10)|from=BEC-E03|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-X03|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=Log-concavity (D5, proof sketch inlined). At chemical potential 0 each excited state's occupation is geometric; convolutions and partial sums keep log-concavity, so E_m^2 >= E_{m-1} E_{m+1} and Z_m^2 >= Z_{m-1} Z_{m+1}. Hence P(N_0 = j) is log-concave in j and the survival ratio P(N_0 >= k+1)/P(N_0 >= k) does not increase with k. Strict inequality is expected (the first excited level alone gives C(m+2,2) q^m, strictly log-concave).|points=every m from 1 to N_max(q) - 1 at the seven grid q|predicted=the non-strict inequalities hold at every m (scored); strict inequality at every m is read and report|verdict_rule=integer cross-multiplication of the scaled integers; MET if no scored inequality fails|method=reader on the X_m and Y_m streams|falsifier=any violation (MISS)|cost=two big products per m; under 3 min|prefreeze=XP4: the inequalities at m <= 2 (from E_0 to E_3 and Z_0 to Z_3) are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 and were evaluated by the final critic (critic/k8_selfconsistency.py); otherwise none (smoke at excluded q, SM1)|from=BC-X08|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-X04|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=The exact-rational cost follows the closed-form bound D_N (D17). Bands: bits(den Z_N) in [bits(D_N) - 3N, bits(D_N)] (the gcd loss was 0 to 2.5N at the excluded q, lane ENGINE and fix-pass f4_x04.py: CONJECTURE); bits(num Z_N) - bits(den Z_N) in [0, ceil(3N log2(b/(b-a))) + 1] (DERIVED from 1 <= Z_N <= Z_1(q)^N); bits(den Var) in [2 bits(D_N) - 6N, 2 bits(D_N) + 2 ceil(3N log2(b/(b-a))) + 2]. At q = 1/1000000, N = 16 both lower bands are widened by the gcd loss that b - a = 999999 = 3^3 7 11 13 37 forces: every c_k is a multiple of b - a, and the sum over primes r dividing b - a of v_r((N!)^2) log2 r is 44.57 bits there, against the 48 bits that 3N allows; each is widened by 45 bits, so the den Var band allows a loss of 141 bits, against about 89 to 103 expected (twice the sum, plus twice the 0 to 7 bits of other primes); at the excluded 1/100000 and 1/10000000 this sum was the whole loss at N = 16 (final critic, critic/k7_varbits.py). Every prime r <= N with d = ord_r(b/a) forces about 2 v_r(floor(N/d)!) log2 r bits (d = 1 for r dividing b - a; at q = 1/1000000 every prime up to 13 that does not divide b has d = 1, so the rule gives the same 44.57 bits; r = 2 adds more where a and b are both odd, which no row q has). This predicts at most 0.79 of 3N at (2/5, 256) and 0.49 at (1/2, 256), so no other point is near its band. These bit lengths set the cost table, including engine B's prime counts (D19).|points=the 29 grid points with N >= 16|predicted=every printed bit length inside its band; bits(D_N) with the numerator-excess bound: q = 2/5: 16: 944 (excess <= 37), 32: 3675 (excess <= 72), 64: 14486 (excess <= 143), 128: 57507 (excess <= 284), 256: 229144 (excess <= 567); q = 1/2: 16: 403 (excess <= 49), 32: 1579 (excess <= 97), 64: 6235 (excess <= 193), 128: 24763 (excess <= 385), 256: 98683 (excess <= 769); q = 3/4: 16: 799 (excess <= 97), 32: 3150 (excess <= 193), 64: 12462 (excess <= 385), 128: 49518 (excess <= 769), 192: 111150 (excess <= 1153), 256: 197358 (excess <= 1537), 384: 443502 (excess <= 2305), 512: 787950 (excess <= 3073); q = 9/10: 16: 1305 (excess <= 161), 32: 5205 (excess <= 320), 64: 20671 (excess <= 639), 128: 82219 (excess <= 1277); q = 99/100: 16: 2522 (excess <= 320), 32: 10229 (excess <= 639), 64: 41028 (excess <= 1277), 128: 163989 (excess <= 2553); q = 999/1000: 16: 3721 (excess <= 480), 32: 15182 (excess <= 958); q = 1/1000000: 16: 8133 (excess <= 2), with the widened bands bits(den Z) in [8040, 8133] and bits(den Var) in [16125, 16270]|verdict_rule=READ3 on exact integers; MET if every bit length lies in its band|method=engines print bits=; the reader compares with the bands|falsifier=a bit length outside its band (MISS)|cost=free (printed with BEC-X01)|prefreeze=COMPUTED: bits(D_N) as exact products at the grid points (this synthesis calc/c8_qN_bits.py; lane ENGINE constants.py and judge-math at N = 256); the bands were checked against 24 excluded measurements (lane ENGINE band_check.txt, all inside); the widening at q = 1/1000000 comes from b - a and N alone (fix-pass f4_x04.py, which also evaluated the sum at all 29 points), and the rule was checked by exact recursions only at the excluded 1/100000, 1/10000000, 43/64, 1/5, 2/9, 3/5 and 2/7 for N = 8, 16, 24: the sum plus 0 to 16 bits from other primes (0 to 7 at N = 16) in den Z, and, in den Var, about twice the sum as q -> 0 (1/100000 and 1/10000000: from 0.04 bits below it to 14.6 above), while elsewhere den Var also gains the numerator excess and its loss was -23 to 117 bits, from 69 bits below twice the sum to 29 above it; the per-prime rule (d = ord_r(b/a)) is verifier round 1's (v7_gcdloss.py, SM10: from a, b and N alone at the 29 points; exact checks only at the excluded 2/7, 3/5, 5/8, 1/5, 2/9, 43/64 and 2/3 for N = 8 to 40), recomputed by second-pass s1_compute.py (SM11: 0.79 of 3N at (2/5, 256), 0.77 at (2/5, 128), 0.49 at (1/2, 256), 0.37 at (3/4, 512), 0.93 at (1/1000000, 16); the forced product divides D_N/den Z_N in all 25 exact cases at the excluded 2/7, 5/8, 2/9, 43/64 and 2/3, with 0 to 7.1 bits more); bits(D_N) and the excess bound rechecked at 5 points and at the CS points by verifier round 1 (v5_multimod.py, v6_spot.py)|from=BEC-E05 (recounted on the union grid)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-L01|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=Grand-canonical bound at the same mean (D5): Var_GC = <N_0>(<N_0>+1) is the variance of a geometric N_0 with the canonical mean; the canonical survival is log-concave and crosses that geometric law once, from above, so Var_C < <N_0>(<N_0>+1) strictly. The ratio R = Var_C/Var_GC is predicted in three regimes: R = 1 - 2 eps (1 + O(N eps)) as q -> 1 (BEC-B02), R N(N+1)/(3q) -> 1 as q -> 0 (BEC-B01), and R from the pole form at fixed q and large N (BEC-L04).|points=GX (62 points)|predicted=Var_C < <N_0>(<N_0>+1) at all 62 points; R read and report at every point|verdict_rule=exact rationals; MET if the strict inequality holds everywhere|method=reader on engine A's <N_0> and Var (equal to B's by BEC-X01)|falsifier=Var_C >= Var_GC anywhere (MISS); PF2 (A prints Var_GC as Var) gives equality and must read NOT_MET|cost=inside the grid run|prefreeze=XP4: the sub-reads at N = 1, 2, 3 at the seven q are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 and were evaluated by the final critic (critic/k8_selfconsistency.py); otherwise none (smoke at excluded q, SM1)|from=BC-X09|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-L02|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=The owner's fixed-q limit (D4): temperature stays fixed in trap units, the fraction goes to 1, <N_ex> stays bounded, and the correction is O(1/N). The canonical N_ex law is the limit law conditioned on N_ex <= N, so <N_ex>_N strictly increases with N and stays below S(q); 1 - f_N = S/N - Delta1/N with Delta1 > 0, so the correction is O(1/N) with the exact coefficient S(q); what is left after it is geometric (BEC-L04). Exactly, Var_N < V(q) when N + 1 - S >= sqrt(V) (D4) or N^2/4 < V (Popoviciu).|points=every N <= N_max(q) at the seven grid q|predicted=<N_ex>_{N+1} > <N_ex>_N at all 1321 consecutive pairs; <N_ex>_N < S_lo(q) at all 1328 values of N, with S from BEC-L03 at the five interior q; at q = 1/1000000 with S and V certified by the reader to an absolute width of 2^-512, finer than BEC-B01's 1e-6 C1 q^(N+1) (2.9e-105 at N = 16), because Delta1 there is about C1 q^(N+1), so a coarse S_lo would fail the read for a correct engine (24 q^4 = 2.4e-23 alone exceeds Delta1 for N >= 4); the values S = 3.000009000013e-6 and V = 3.000012000019e-6 are for display only; and S > 1/(1-q)^3 - 1 = 999999999 at q = 999/1000; Var_N < V(q) wherever D4 or Popoviciu applies: q = 2/5: Popoviciu for N <= 5, D4 for N >= 7; q = 1/2: Popoviciu for N <= 7, D4 for N >= 12; q = 3/4: Popoviciu for N <= 23, D4 for N >= 95; q = 9/10: Popoviciu for N <= 90, D4 for N >= 1314; q = 99/100: Popoviciu for N <= 2627, D4 for N >= 1210264 (every N at 999/1000 and 1/1000000), which covers every grid N except (1/2, 8), (3/4, 32), (3/4, 64) and (9/10, 128) (those are conjectured in BEC-L06)|verdict_rule=exact rationals against certified constants; MET if every claim holds|method=reader on engine A's every-N output; S, V certified as in BEC-L03|falsifier=a decrease, <N_ex>_N >= S_lo, or Var_N >= V at a listed point (MISS)|cost=inside the grid run; reader seconds|prefreeze=COMPUTED: S, V and the thresholds from closed forms (XP5); identities checked only at excluded q (SM1, SM2); XP4: the sub-reads at N <= 3 (the rise from N = 1 to 3, <N_ex>_N < S and Var_N < V at N <= 3) are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 and were evaluated by the final critic (critic/k8_selfconsistency.py); final critic k3 (SM8, XP5); verifier round 1 v6_spot.py (SM10: the thresholds at the five q)|from=BC-X10, BC-X14 (Var below V), SC-F01|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-L03|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=The fixed-q limit constants S(q) (mean of the limit law; lane SCALING's nu) and V(q) (its variance; kappa2), certified by the reader in outward-rounded dyadic sums (2^-512) with the closed-form tails 3y <= (1-y)^-3 - 1 <= 3y/(1-y)^3 and [T, T/(1-q^K)^2], T = sum_{n>=K} g_n q^n. N(1 - f_N) -> S and Var(N_0) -> V. These reads certify arithmetic: they are fixed once the formulas are frozen.|points=q in {2/5, 1/2, 3/4, 9/10, 99/100}|predicted=q = 2/5: S in [4.669153422091204393452538241920, 4.669153422091204393452538241921], V in [6.280122848908250875914446002650, 6.280122848908250875914446002651]; q = 1/2: S in [9.272388574999977861520186371511, 9.272388574999977861520186371512], V in [13.241934423539872859657115442336, 13.241934423539872859657115442337]; q = 3/4: S in [84.197380903459504956974480568946, 84.197380903459504956974480568947], V in [135.425725091207629283180178856423, 135.425725091207629283180178856424]; q = 9/10: S in [1269.665919018726117008134841139587, 1269.665919018726117008134841139588], V in [2044.587954181067747987370462088794, 2044.587954181067747987370462088795]; q = 99/100: S in [1208950.314750057330432814465273403134, 1208950.314750057330432814465273403135], V in [1725837.209433678256977766247415156483, 1725837.209433678256977766247415156484]; each reader interval lies inside its 30-digit interval|verdict_rule=READ3; MET if every certified interval lies inside its band|method=tools/read.py constants (K about 400 at 2/5 and 1/2, 900 at 3/4, 1500 at 9/10, 14000 at 99/100)|falsifier=a certified interval outside its band (MISS)|cost=under 1 min|prefreeze=COMPUTED: certified sums at the five q (lane EXACT constants_rowq.py, lane SCALING fixedq.py, judge-math j3_limits.py, this synthesis calc/c3_limits.py; S and V at 1/2, 3/4, 9/10, 99/100 agree with the lanes to every printed digit); final critic k3 (SM8, XP5); verifier round 1 v2_gap.py (SM10: S and V at 2/5, 1/2 and 3/4)|from=BC-X14 (constants), SC-F01 (constants)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-L04|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Approach to the fixed-q limit: the pole form (D8). pi(m) = (G/2) q^m [(m+1)(m+2) - (2m+3) mu1 + mu2] (1 + O(m^3 q^m)), inserted in the exact D4 sums, predicts Delta1 = S - <N_ex>_N and Delta2 = V - Var_N, hence <N_0> = N - S + Delta1, Var = V - Delta2, R and F. The approach is geometric, Delta1 ~ (G q/(2(1-q))) N^3 q^N. Designed contrast (lane SCALING's planted reading, not the owner's): an algebraic tail c/N with c != 0 would need N2 Delta1(N2) >= (1/2) N1 Delta1(N1) at consecutive ladder points; the frozen ratios are far below 1/2 (fixed once the Delta1 reads are MET, so not a negative control). Also 0 < q/(1-q) - lambda_1 < Delta1/3, exactly (D10: the e = 1 term of Delta1 = sum_e g_e (q^e/(1-q^e)) E[q^(e N_0)] is 3 times the gap).|points=ladders: q = 2/5 at N in {16, 32, 64, 128, 256}; q = 1/2 at {32, 48, 64, 96, 128, 256}; q = 3/4 at {192, 256, 384, 512}; one-step ratios also use N+1|predicted=constants (G; mu1; mu2 - mu1^2; C2/H(1)): q = 2/5: 17.24436954696; 8.062324217517; 11.18018366675; -11.308. q = 1/2: 120.2913972443; 15.22981276859; 22.78257986743; -416.54. q = 3/4: 6.423273589777e9; 115.5472552893; 205.9030578960; -1.1157e13. Delta1 (Delta2), the error estimate est and the band on Delta/pole, band = max(100 est, 1e-9) rounded up: q = 2/5: N = 16: 0.004411868682 (0.05667963797), est 0.000332, band 1 +/- 0.04; N = 32: 2.302519129e-8 (6.656731143e-7), est 1.14e-9, band 1 +/- 2e-7; N = 64: 4.184877917e-20 (2.550787441e-18), est 1.68e-21, band 1 +/- 1e-9; N = 128: 1.262005562e-44 (1.577187846e-42), est 4.58e-46, band 1 +/- 1e-9; N = 256: 1.229721407e-94 (3.111023665e-92), est 4.24e-96, band 1 +/- 1e-9. q = 1/2: N = 32: 0.0001519950392 (0.003723987074), est 5.30e-5, band 1 +/- 0.006; N = 48: 1.169440721e-8 (4.744812849e-7), est 2.73e-9, band 1 +/- 3e-7; N = 64: 5.105832372e-13 (2.890505962e-11), est 9.87e-14, band 1 +/- 1e-9; N = 96: 4.802473848e-22 (4.257429065e-20),