PREDICT|id=BEC-L05|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=S and V as asymptotic series in x = ln(1/q) (D9). The first two terms of S are the owner's N_ex formula; the third writes out the owner's O(x^-1 log(1/x)) piece as x^-1 (ln(1/x) + gamma - 19/24). The series use the residues through s = -3 (S) and s = -2 (V); the next residue gives the first omitted term, which sets the band (10 times it). The series diverge for every x > 0, so the bands are not proven bounds. V's leading term zeta(2) x^-3 = (zeta(2)/zeta(3)) N t^3 at t^3 = zeta(3)/(N x^3), the REPORTED canonical-fluctuation scaling (BECCITE R1, R2; verified=0). No engine output enters: the row certifies the reader's constants and series, and it carries the planted reader fault PF7.|points=q in {2/5, 1/2, 3/4, 9/10, 99/100}|predicted=read and report: S - Mellin_S = -4.0397e-8, -9.9949e-9, -1.2287e-10, -8.0933e-13, -6.3917e-18; V - Mellin_V = 7.1632e-7, 2.3132e-7, 6.7617e-9, 1.2133e-10, 1.0042e-14; the owner's two-term value against S: 2/5: 4.501340 against S = 4.669153, 1/2: 8.745085 against S = 9.272389, 3/4: 80.30140 against S = 84.19738, 9/10: 1250.031 against S = 1269.666, 99/100: 1208514 against S = 1208950. Scored: abs(S - Mellin_S) <= 5e-7, 1e-7, 2e-9, 9e-12, 7e-17 and abs(V - Mellin_V) <= 7e-6, 3e-6, 7e-8, 2e-9, 2e-13|verdict_rule=READ3 on certified residual intervals; MET if every interval lies in its band; PF7 must read NOT_MET|method=reader: certified x (BEC-K02), gamma, zeta(2), zeta(3) (BEC-K01) and S, V (BEC-L03); the series evaluated in outward rationals|falsifier=a residual interval outside its band (MISS); NOT_MEASURED if the certified constants are unavailable (rule STOP); PF7 (drop -19/24) shifts the S series by 19/(24x) = 0.864, 1.14, 2.75, 7.51, 78.8 and must read NOT_MET|cost=seconds|prefreeze=COMPUTED: the residuals at the row q (lane EXACT constants_rowq.py at 1/2, 9/10, 99/100; this synthesis calc/c5_mellin_fixedq.py at all five, in certified rationals); smoke at excluded q 1/5, 3/5, 199/200 (SM1); final critic k3 (SM8, XP5); verifier round 1 v6_spot.py (SM10: the PF7 shifts and two-term values at the five q)|from=BC-X16|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-L06|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=Monotonicity claims the exact rows do not prove. (a) f_N strictly increases with N at fixed q, so f_N >= (1-q)^3 = f_1. (b) Var(N_0) strictly increases with N at fixed q. (c) Every survival P(N_0 >= k), and hence <N_0>, strictly decreases as q rises at fixed N; proved for N <= 6 by Sturm sequences (D11), conjectured above. (d) Var_N < V(q) at the four grid points that BEC-L02 does not cover. Var(N_0) itself is not monotone in q: at N = 1 it is p(1-p), peaked at (1-q)^3 = 1/2.|points=(a), (b): every N <= N_max(q) at the seven grid q. (c): across 1/1000000 < 2/5 < 1/2 < 3/4 < 9/10 < 99/100 < 999/1000 at N in {1, 2, 3, 8, 16}; across 2/5, 1/2, 3/4, 9/10, 99/100, 999/1000 at N = 32; across 2/5, 1/2, 3/4, 9/10, 99/100 at N in {4, 64, 128}; 2/5 < 1/2 < 3/4 at N = 256. (d): (1/2, 8), (3/4, 32), (3/4, 64), (9/10, 128)|predicted=every strict inequality holds; at N = 1, Var(1/1000000) < Var(2/5) > Var(1/2) (from BEC-C01)|verdict_rule=integer comparisons of reduced fractions and certified V; MET if every scored comparison holds|method=reader|falsifier=a reversed or equal pair (MISS), a real NOT_MET; a reversal in (c) at N <= 6 would contradict D11 and point to an engine fault|cost=comparisons only|prefreeze=COMPUTED symbolically: the recursion as rational functions of q for N <= 6 (lane EXACT mono_sturm.py), used only for the Sturm proofs; its only numeric evaluation was a sign probe at the excluded q = 1/5; it fixes the N = 4 values but was never evaluated at a row q (XP3); smoke at four excluded q to N = 24 (SM1); XP4: the sub-reads (a) and (b) for the steps from N = 1 to 2 and 2 to 3, and (c) at N in {1, 2, 3}, are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 and were evaluated by the final critic (critic/k8_selfconsistency.py); a possible route to (d): truncating a log-concave law (D5) may lower its variance; with a checked proof or citation for the discrete case, filed in a dated addendum, (d) could become DERIVED; this freeze has neither|from=BC-X11 (q chain with 2/5 and 3/4; (d) recomputed on the union grid)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-B01|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=Boundary q -> 0 (D6). Every boson goes to the ground state: Z_N -> 1, <N_0> -> N, Var -> 0, P(N_0 = N) -> 1. The q-series of <N_ex>_N and S agree through q^N; S - <N_ex>_N = C1 q^(N+1) (1 + O(q)) with C1 = (N+1)(N+2)(N+3)/2 and V - Var_N = C2 q^(N+1) (1 + O(q)) with C2 = (N+1)^2 (N+2)(N+3)/2; also Var_N/(3q) -> 1 and R N(N+1)/(3q) -> 1. The limits and the bound P(N_0 = N) > 1 - S are derived; the O(q) bands are estimates.|points=q = 1/1000000 at N in {1, 2, 3, 8, 16}|predicted=C1 = 12, 30, 60, 495, 2907; C2 = 24, 90, 240, 4455, 49419; each of (S - <N_ex>_N)/(C1 q^(N+1)), (V - Var_N)/(C2 q^(N+1)), Var_N/(3q) and R N(N+1)/(3q) lies in [1 - 1e-4, 1 + 1e-4] (at the excluded q = 1/100000 the O(q) coefficients were at most 6.5, and judge-math found the same at 1/10^7); scored (DERIVED): 1 - P(N_0 = N) = 1 - 1/Z_N < S(1/1000000) and <N_0> > N - S at every listed N, with S certified to 2^-512 (S = 3.000009000013e-6 is for display only)|verdict_rule=READ3 on certified ratio intervals; MET if every interval lies in its band and both bounds hold|method=exact rationals from both engines; the reader certifies S and V to an absolute width below 1e-6 C1 q^(N+1)|falsifier=a ratio interval outside its band, or a bound violated (MISS)|cost=seconds (Z_16 at q = 1/10^6 is about 8k bits)|prefreeze=COMPUTED: the integers C1, C2 and S, V at 1/1000000 (closed forms; this synthesis calc/c6_boundary.py); smoke at excluded 1/100000 (SM1) and 1/10^7 (SM4); XP4: the sub-reads at N in {1, 2, 3} are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 and were evaluated by the final critic (critic/k8_selfconsistency.py); the integers C1 and C2 recounted by the final critic (k6, SM8) and verifier round 1 (v6_spot.py, SM10)|from=BC-X12|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-B02|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=Boundary q -> 1 (D7). At fixed N the gas turns classical: with eps = (1-q)^3, <N_0> -> 0 like N eps and P(N_0 = 0) -> 1; R -> 1 and Var/<N_0> -> 1, so canonical and grand-canonical fluctuations agree to leading order. The expansion parameter is eps, not 1-q. (a) <N_0>/(N eps) - 1 = (N-1)(1 - (1+q)^-3) eps (1 + r1); (b) 1 - R = 2 eps (1 + r2) at every N; (c) Var/<N_0> - 1 = (N-2) eps (1 + r3) for N != 2 (exactly -eps at N = 1; N = 2 is exact in BEC-C02). The coefficients are derived; the r bands are estimates.|points=q = 999/1000 at N in {1, 2, 3, 8, 16, 32}; q = 99/100 at N in {1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128}; q = 9/10 at N in {1, 2, 3, 4, 8}|predicted=(a): q = 999/1000 (coefficient 6988005999/7988005999): 0, 8.7481231e-10, 1.7496246e-9, 6.1236862e-9, 1.3122185e-8, 2.7119182e-8; q = 99/100 (coefficient 6880599/7880599): 0, 8.7310609e-7, 1.7462122e-6, 2.6193183e-6, 6.1117426e-6, 1.3096591e-5, 2.7066289e-5, 5.5005684e-5, 0.00011088447; q = 9/10 (coefficient 5859/6859): 0, 0.00085420615, 0.0017084123, 0.0025626185, 0.0059794431; (b) 1 - R = 2e-9, 2e-6, 2e-3 times (1 + r2); (c) (N-2) eps (1 + r3); bands abs(r) <= 1e-5 at 999/1000, 5e-3 at 99/100, 1e-1 at 9/10; the N = 1 reads are exact: the (a) term is 0, 1 - R = 2 eps/(1+eps), Var/<N_0> - 1 = -eps|verdict_rule=exact rationals; MET if every ratio lies in its band and the N = 1 reads are exact|method=reader on both engines' output|falsifier=a ratio outside its band (MISS)|cost=seconds beyond the grid run|prefreeze=COMPUTED: the derived coefficients at the row q (lane EXACT boundary_rowq.py; this synthesis calc/c6_boundary.py); smoke at excluded 199/200 (r up to 1.75 N eps, SM1) and 49/50, 1999/2000 (r up to 1.6 N eps, SM4); the N = 4 values at 99/100 and 9/10 are fixed by the symbolic forms, never evaluated (XP3); XP4: the sub-reads at N in {1, 2, 3} (r1, r2, r3 and the exact N = 1 reads) are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 and were evaluated by the final critic (critic/k8_selfconsistency.py); final critic k3 (SM8, XP5); verifier round 1 v6_spot.py (SM10: the coefficients and the (a) values)|from=BC-X13|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-O01|kind=OBSERVABLE|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=One-body coherence, kept apart from occupation and variance (D10). The one-body density matrix is diagonal in the oscillator basis; each level-e state has eigenvalue lambda_e = sum_k q^(k e) Z_{N-k}/Z_N = (q^e/(1-q^e))(1 - E[q^(e N_0)]). lambda_0 = <N_0> is the largest eigenvalue (Penrose-Onsager) and lambda_e strictly decreases with e. The excited trace equals N - <N_0>. At fixed q, lambda_e -> q^e/(1-q^e) from below while lambda_0 grows like N: one macroscopic eigenvalue. A third, brute-force construction enumerates a truncated model (levels e <= L) state by state.|points=GX at the grid N with e in {1, 2, 3}; TRUNC (48 runs); TC and the TS points (7/10, 8) and (9/10, 16) (one scored inequality); the other 8 TS points (read and report)|predicted=lambda_e from engine A's survival sums equals (q^e/(1-q^e))(1 - E[q^(e N_0)]) from engine B's distribution, exactly; lambda_0 = <N_0> byte for byte; lambda_0 > lambda_1 > lambda_2 > lambda_3; the excited trace equals N - <N_0> exactly; in the truncated model the enumerated Z_N equals the truncated recursion, there are 0 off-diagonal one-body elements, the largest diagonal entry is <N_0> and every diagonal entry equals the survival formula; at TC, (7/10, 8) and (9/10, 16) the interval engine's lambda_1 bracket lies below q_hi/(1-q_hi) (scored); there Jensen's inequality (q^n is convex in n) gives gap = (q/(1-q)) E[q^(N_0)] >= (q/(1-q)) q^<N_0>, about 0.09, 1.7e-21 and 1.2e-19 from the frozen f values (the Gaussian f of BEC-T11 at TC, f_as of BEC-T04 at the two TS points), while the p = 128 lambda_1 bracket is at most about 2.5e-32, 1.8e-32 and 2.8e-30 wide by the D13 first-order form, a margin of about 4e30, 1e11 and 4e10; at the other 8 TS points the same bound lies about 15 to 3250 orders of magnitude below the bracket width, so a correct engine's bracket may overlap q_hi/(1-q_hi) and the inequality there is read and report; lambda_0/lambda_1 is read and report at every scaling point; the reader prints the certified bound (q_lo/(1-q_lo)) q_lo^(N f_hi), from the engine's own f bracket, beside the printed bracket width at every scaling point|verdict_rule=exact rationals; READ3 at TC, (7/10, 8) and (9/10, 16); MET if every scored identity and inequality holds|method=reader on both engines; the truncated model lists multisets of modes with weight q^E; interval engine A prints lambda_1 with opposite endpoints|falsifier=any identity broken, an off-diagonal element, or, at TC, (7/10, 8) or (9/10, 16), a lambda_1 bracket reaching q_hi/(1-q_hi) (MISS)|cost=seconds for the truncated model, O(N) per e per grid point|prefreeze=none at row points for the exact reads (SM1 truncated brute force at excluded 1/5, 3/5); XP4: the eigenvalue order at N <= 3 is fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 (no seat evaluated it); the scaling-point sizes come from frozen values only and the D13 form (fix-pass f3_o01.py); the TRUNC mode and state counts rechecked by verifier round 1 (v6_spot.py, SM10)|from=BC-X17 (plus a scaling-point read, judge-design optional item)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-O02|kind=OBSERVABLE|tag=DERIVED|control=NEGATIVE (PF9)|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Number conservation fixes <a_0> = 0 (D10). The canonical state lives in the N-boson sector and a_0 maps it into the (N-1)-boson sector, so <a_0> = Tr(rho_N a_0) = 0 exactly at every N and q, even when lambda_0 = <N_0> is macroscopic. Finite-N occupation is not spontaneous phase-symmetry breaking: abs(<a_0>)^2 = 0, not <N_0>. A coherent state with the same mean would have <a_0> != 0 and Poisson statistics (BEC-G02). The receipt audit lives in BEC-N06. Planted control PF9 shows that the trace check can fail: the same truncated-trace routine is fed the ground-mode coherent state with alpha^2 = <N_0> of the same TRUNC run, cut to 0..N bosons and normalized. Its entries are irrational, so the routine takes each ground-mode entry in the exact form rho_(m,n) = alpha^(m+n) r_(m,n)/sqrt(m! n!), with rational r_(m,n) and rational alpha^2 (here every r_(m,n) = 1/s_N, s_K = sum_{n=0..K} alpha^(2n)/n!; for the canonical state every r_(m,n) with m != n is 0). Since (n-1)! n! = n ((n-1)!)^2, rho_(n,n-1) sqrt(n) = alpha^(2n-1) r_(n,n-1)/(n-1)!, so Tr(rho a_0) is alpha times a rational and abs(Tr(rho a_0))^2 is evaluated in rationals of alpha^2. Here it is alpha^2 (s_(N-1)/s_N)^2, a positive rational (for example 8/81 at q = 1/2, N = 1, where alpha^2 = 1/8), and the read must be MISS.|points=every receipt; TRUNC (48 runs)|predicted=the reader prints a0 = 0 as an exact structural value with this reason and computes no phase; the truncated Tr(rho_N a_0), over Fock states with 0..N bosons, is exactly 0 in all 48 runs; PF9: the planted coherent state gives a positive abs(Tr(rho a_0))^2 and reads MISS in all 48 runs (designed NOT_MET on the planted copy)|verdict_rule=MET if a0 = 0 everywhere, every truncated trace of the canonical state is 0 and the PF9 copy reads MISS|method=reader; truncated trace in exact rationals (PF9 in rationals of alpha^2)|falsifier=a nonzero <a_0> or a nonzero truncated trace of the canonical state (MISS), or a PF9 copy that does not read MISS (the check does not bite)|cost=seconds|prefreeze=none (SM1 at excluded q); the PF9 value 8/81 is a hand evaluation from the frozen BEC-C01 value <N_0> = 1/8 (XP4); rechecked by verifier round 1 (v6_spot.py, SM10) and second-pass s1_compute.py (SM11)|from=BC-X18 (structural part)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-G01|kind=CONTRAST|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=The grand-canonical fluctuation law tested on the canonical output. Claim GC: abs(R - 1) <= 1/2. On the condensed side it fails, and the failure is fixed by inputs: Var_C < V(q) and <N_0> > N - S(q) (BEC-L02, BEC-L03) give R < V/((N-S)(N-S+1)) < 1/2; these designed NOT_MET sub-reads certify arithmetic and are not negative controls. On the classical side GC holds by BEC-B02 (R = 1 - 2 eps to first order); those sub-reads are conjectural.|points=condensed: q = 2/5 at N in {16, 32, 64, 128, 256}; q = 1/2 at {32, 64, 128, 256}; q = 3/4 at {192, 256, 384, 512}. Classical: q = 99/100 at N in {1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128}; q = 999/1000 at {1, 2, 3, 8, 16, 32}; q = 9/10 at {1, 2, 3, 4, 8}. R read and report at every other grid point|predicted=GC NOT_MET by design at all 13 condensed points, with R from the pole values and the closed-form bound: q = 2/5: 16: R 0.04451 (bound 0.04495), 32: R 0.008111 (bound 0.008111), 64: R 0.001754 (bound 0.001754), 128: R 0.0004096 (bound 0.0004096), 256: R 9.903e-5 (bound 9.903e-5); q = 1/2: 32: R 0.02455 (bound 0.02456), 64: R 0.004342 (bound 0.004342), 128: R 0.0009315 (bound 0.0009315), 256: R 0.0002167 (bound 0.0002167); q = 3/4: 192: R 0.01155 (bound 0.01155), 256: R 0.004562 (bound 0.004562), 384: R 0.001502 (bound 0.001502), 512: R 0.0007382 (bound 0.0007382); GC MET at all 20 classical points (R = 1 - 2e-6, 1 - 2e-9 and 1 - 2e-3 to first order)|verdict_rule=MET if exactly this pattern of sub-verdicts occurs|method=exact rationals; R as an exact rational|falsifier=GC holding at a condensed point, or failing at a classical point|cost=none beyond the grid run|prefreeze=COMPUTED: R from the BEC-L04 pole values and the BEC-B02 coefficients (closed forms); the N = 4 value at 99/100 and 9/10 is fixed by the symbolic forms, never evaluated (XP3); XP4: the classical sub-reads at N in {1, 2, 3} are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 and were evaluated by the final critic (critic/k8_selfconsistency.py), so the fixed sub-reads are the 13 condensed ones and these 9; final critic k3 (SM8, XP5); verifier round 1 (SM10: R at the ladder points in v2_gap.py, the bound at (2/5, 16) in v6_spot.py)|from=BC-X19|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-G02|kind=CONTRAST|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=The coherent-state (Poisson) law tested on the canonical output. Claim P: the Fano factor F = Var_C/<N_0> lies in [1/2, 2]. At fixed q the condensate is number-squeezed: F < V/(N - S) -> 0, so P fails where V/(N - S) < 1/2 (fixed by inputs). Where V/(N - S) >= 1/2 the outcome rests on the pole values (conjectural). In the classical limit F = 1 + (N-2) eps (BEC-B02), so P holds. The canonical condensate is neither grand-canonical nor coherent.|points=q = 2/5 at N in {16, 32, 64, 128, 256}; q = 1/2 at {32, 64, 128, 256}; q = 3/4 at {192, 256, 384, 512}; and the 20 classical points of BEC-G01|predicted=F with the bound V/(N - S): q = 2/5: 16: F 0.5490 (V/(N-S) 0.5543), 32: F 0.2298 (V/(N-S) 0.2298), 64: F 0.1058 (V/(N-S) 0.1058), 128: F 0.05092 (V/(N-S) 0.05092), 256: F 0.02499 (V/(N-S) 0.02499); q = 1/2: 32: F 0.5825 (V/(N-S) 0.5826), 64: F 0.2420 (V/(N-S) 0.2420), 128: F 0.1115 (V/(N-S) 0.1115), 256: F 0.05367 (V/(N-S) 0.05367); q = 3/4: 192: F 1.256 (V/(N-S) 1.256), 256: F 0.7883 (V/(N-S) 0.7883), 384: F 0.4517 (V/(N-S) 0.4517), 512: F 0.3166 (V/(N-S) 0.3166); so P is MET at (2/5, 16), (1/2, 32), (3/4, 192) and (3/4, 256) (conjectural sub-reads; the thinnest margin is (2/5, 16) at 0.549 against 1/2, with a pole band of 1e-3 on Var) and NOT_MET by design at the other 9 condensed points (fixed by inputs); P MET at the 20 classical points (F within 1.3e-4 of 1 at 99/100; F = 1.006 at (9/10, 8))|verdict_rule=MET if exactly this pattern of sub-verdicts occurs|method=exact rationals|falsifier=P holding at a NOT_MET point, or failing at a MET point|cost=none beyond the grid run|prefreeze=COMPUTED: F from BEC-L04 and BEC-B02 (closed forms); (2/5, 16) is unexposed (XP8); N = 4 as in BEC-G01 (XP3); XP4: the classical sub-reads at N in {1, 2, 3} are fixed by BEC-C01 to C03 and were evaluated by the final critic (critic/k8_selfconsistency.py), so they join the 9 condensed sub-reads fixed by inputs; final critic k3 (SM8, XP5); verifier round 1 (SM10: F at the ladder points in v2_gap.py, the bound at (2/5, 16) in v6_spot.py)|from=BC-X20 (points listed explicitly)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T01|kind=NUMERICS|tag=DERIVED|control=NEGATIVE (planted a, b)|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Precision of the certified scaling bracket, one interval design (D13). Production p = 128 in engine A at every TS and TC point and in engine B at N <= 32768. Both recursions run in both passes; all terms are positive; f takes numerator and denominator from opposite passes, so no monotonicity in q is used. W_N <= W_bound = f u (36N/x + 2N^2 + 36N + 4), u = 2^(1-p), first order, rigorous with u/(1 - (N^2+8N)u). D13 derives this bound for construction 1, which gives engine A's f bracket. Engine B's interval mode runs construction 2, for which D13 derives no bound, so engine B's W_N/W_bound and its crit are read and report here; BEC-N03 scores engine B's widths against engine A's (lane ENGINE measured an E/Z width ratio of 0.97 to 1.04 at the excluded t = 5/7). The owner's precision target N^(1/3) W_N < 1/1000 is a numerical precision criterion, not a claim about the asymptotic remainder, and it is read only here and in BEC-T02. p_req is the least p with N^(1/3) W_bound < 1/1000. The reader evaluates W_bound and p_req with the engine's certified f_hi from the p = 128 run, never with an estimate; this matters at TC, where the Mellin f_as = 0.027 does not apply (BEC-T10, T11). Planted faults: (a) round to nearest in both passes; (b) c_k replaced by (1-q^k)^-3, dropping the -1, in the interval construction 2.|points=TS and TC at p = 128; at p = p_req for n <= 32 (9 points); planted (a) at DY (q = 1/2 and 3/4, N = 16, 64); planted (b) at TC and TS (1/2, 8)|predicted=p_req: (1/2, 8) 33, (1/2, 16) 40, (1/2, 32) 47, (1/2, 64) 54, (7/10, 8) 33, (7/10, 16) 40, (7/10, 32) 47, (7/10, 64) 54, (9/10, 8) 30, (9/10, 16) 38, (9/10, 32) 45, where the TC value is set by the reader from f_hi and is read and report: 29 if f_hi < 0.050266, 30 if f_hi < 0.100532, 31 if f_hi < 0.201064; the corrected Gaussian estimate f = 0.0557 gives 30; at p = 128, N^(1/3) W_N <= N^(1/3) W_bound = 2.30e-32, 2.74e-30, 3.49e-28, 4.49e-26, 1.53e-32, 1.94e-30, 2.54e-28, 3.32e-26, 1.75e-33 (at f = 0.0557), 5.12e-31, 8.74e-29 (same order as the list of p_req), so the target is predicted to be met with a margin above 1e22; at p_req (n <= 32), N^(1/3) W_N < 1/1000 at all 9, bound 0.00091, 0.00085, 0.00084, 0.00061, 0.00060, 0.00061, 0.00055 (at f = 0.0557), 0.00063, 0.00085; W_N/W_bound lies in (0, 1] in every engine A run (its value read and report; expected 0.01 to 0.2); engine B's W_N/W_bound and crit at N <= 32768 are read and report; the Z_m bracket and the sum_{i<=m} E_i bracket overlap at every m; the crit magnitude is read and report (lane ENGINE's extrapolation of 1e-33 at N = 512 and 1e-27 at N = 262144 kept beside). Planted (a): zero-width brackets that miss the exact rational (a non-dyadic rational cannot lie in a zero-width dyadic bracket); planted (b): disjoint Z and sum E brackets at every N >= 1|verdict_rule=READ3 and exact comparisons; MET if every scored bound and target (engine A) holds in the clean runs and both planted faults are detected|method=bec-a scaling --t a/b --n n --p P and bec-a interval at DY; bec_b.py scaling at N <= 32768; the reader evaluates W_bound and crit in rationals|falsifier=W_N above the rigorous bound in an engine A run, the target missed by engine A at p = 128 or p_req, a Z against sum E non-overlap in a clean run, or a planted fault undetected (NOT_MET)|cost=engine A interval: 4 N(N+1)/2 term updates per point (two recursions, two passes): at N = 262144 about 1.4e11, i.e. 23 to 69 min of CPU at the design target of 10 to 30 ns per update (fixed 128-bit mantissa; UNVERIFIED, rule BUDGET), 6 to 17 min wall on 4 cores; at lane ENGINE's pessimistic 0.1 to 0.3 us per update, 1 to 3 h wall per point, still inside a 6 h dispatch job with one point per job; N = 32768: 21 to 64 s of CPU; N <= 4096: under 2 s; p_req reruns 65 to 196 s of CPU in all (the three N = 32768 points dominate; about a quarter of that as wall time on 4 cores); engine B (measured 2.1 us per term, one recursion): 19 min per N = 32768 point, 18 s at N = 4096|prefreeze=COMPUTED: p_req and W_bound from the closed-form bound with the Mellin f (lane SCALING design.py; this synthesis calc/c7_scaling.py, nums.py); at TC recomputed with the corrected Gaussian f = 0.0557 and the f_hi thresholds 0.050266, 0.100532 and 0.201064 for p_req = 29, 30 and 31, and the rerun costs (fix-pass f2_precision.py); the earlier TC values 8.46e-34 and 29 used f_as = 0.027; the bound and fault (a) were exercised only by scratch prototypes at excluded points (t = 3/5, 4/5, 5/7; q = 43/64, 5/8): W/W_bound = 0.030 to 0.151, nearest rounding gave zero width and missed the exact value; final critic k4 (SM8, XP5: the Mellin f and the bound at every TS and TC point); verifier round 1 (SM10: v3_gauss.py, W_bound and the p_req thresholds at TC; v4_certified.py, N^(1/3) W_bound, p_req and the bound at p_req at the 11 points from the frozen f values)|from=SC-T01 (p = 128 production; p_req reruns at n <= 32), BEC-E08 (target; magnitude band now read and report)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T02|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=NEGATIVE|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Designed NOT_MET width controls: the width check must be able to fail. (i) p = p_req - 16 at the 9 points with n <= 32: there (N^2 + 8N) u is 1.0 to 32.5, so neither the first-order bound nor the rigorous form of D13 applies; the first-order value N^(1/3) W_bound = 36.3 to 59.6 only indicates the size, and the designed outcome is crit > 1/1000, a NOT_MET of the target; lane ENGINE's p = 16 run at (1/2, 512) is this control at p_req - 17 and is folded in. (ii) Loose q bracket: engine A reruns (1/2, 4096) and (7/10, 4096) with q_lo multiplied by (1 - 2^-20); the width becomes about 2 f <E> 2^-20 (D18). (iii) Soundness under both: every low-precision or loose bracket intersects the production bracket, since both contain the true value.|points=(i) p_req - 16 = (1/2, 8) 17, (1/2, 16) 24, (1/2, 32) 31, (7/10, 8) 17, (7/10, 16) 24, (7/10, 32) 31, (9/10, 8) 14 (p_req - 16 for the reader's TC p_req, predicted 30), (9/10, 16) 22, (9/10, 32) 29 at those points; (ii) (1/2, 4096) and (7/10, 4096) with --qwiden 20|predicted=(i) crit > 1/1000 at all 9 (designed NOT_MET; no size is predicted); (ii) crit about 0.27 and 0.71, each in [0.05, 4], target NOT_MET by design at both, while BEC-N02 stays MET on the loose brackets; (iii) all 11 intersections hold (rule INTERSECT)|verdict_rule=MET if every designed NOT_MET occurs and every intersection holds|method=bec-a scaling --p P and --qwiden 20; reader as BEC-T01|falsifier=the target reading MET at any designed point (the check does not bite), a crit in (ii) outside [0.05, 4], or a disjoint pair (a soundness failure)|cost=66 to 198 s of CPU in all (the three N = 32768 points of (i) dominate)|prefreeze=COMPUTED: (i) from the bound (calc/c7_scaling.py; TC, the (N^2 + 8N) u range and the costs recomputed by fix-pass f2_precision.py); (ii) from the asymptotic width estimate (lane ENGINE D8; 0.53 against 0.59 measured at excluded (5/7, 3375)); p = 16 at excluded t = 5/7 gave crit 1.3e-2, 0.30, 2.6, 57 at N = 27, 125, 343, 1000; verifier round 1 v4_certified.py (SM10) and second-pass s1_compute.py (SM11): (N^2 + 8N) u at p_req - 16 is 1.0 to 32.5 at the 9 points with n <= 32, and 0.5 to 65 with the n = 64 points and TC at the old p = 13 (the critic's set)|from=SC-T01 (c), BEC-E11, BEC-E12|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T03|kind=MODEL_EXACT|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=The fixed-q identity also holds at the scaling points (D4, D12): <N_ex>_N = S(q_N) - Delta1 and Var_N = V(q_N) - Delta2 with 0 < Delta1 <= B1 and 0 < Delta2 <= B2 (Chernoff). S and V rise with q, so [S(q_lo)_lo - B1, S(q_hi)_hi] and [V(q_lo)_lo - B2, V(q_hi)_hi] are closed-form enclosures of <N_ex>_N and Var_N. They are far narrower than the engine brackets, so the read is an intersection (rule INTERSECT), not containment. This certifies <N_0> and Var(N_0) at the scaling points without the Mellin expansion.|points=TS (10 points); at TC only <N_ex>_N <= S(q_hi)_hi (B1 > 1 there, and Var_N < V is not covered by D4 at TC, so the Var side is read and report)|predicted=ln B1 <= -84.0, -392.0, -1653.5, -6751.5, -28.7, -183.1, -839.5, -3534.7, -17.2, -196.4 and ln B2 <= -78.4, -385.1, -1644.9, -6740.9, -22.5, -175.4, -830.0, -3523.2, -8.9, -186.1 at the 10 TS points in the TS order (float design values rounded up; each certified ln B must lie below its frozen value plus 1); every intersection holds; the depth of the closed-form band inside the engine bracket is read and report|verdict_rule=rule INTERSECT for the enclosures; READ3 for the ln B ceilings; MET if all hold|method=reader: S and V at q_lo and q_hi (about 100/x terms plus tails); B1, B2 at rational z just below exp(theta), theta in {x/4, x/2, 3x/4, 9x/10}, smallest kept, outward rounding|falsifier=a disjoint pair or a certified ln B above its ceiling (NOT_MET)|cost=under 1 s per point beyond BEC-T01|prefreeze=COMPUTED: ln B1, ln B2 in floats at the row points (lane SCALING design.py; judge-math j6_scaling.py at four points; this synthesis calc/c7_scaling.py, nums.py); the series S(e^-x), V(e^-x) at the x of 6 TS points and TC were evaluated by lane SCALING's calibration (XP2); not at t = 7/10; final critic k4 (SM8: ln B1 and ln B2 at four exposed points); verifier round 1 v6_spot.py (SM10: ln B1 at (1/2, 8), XP2)|from=SC-T02 (restated as an intersection read)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T04|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=The leading correction with its drift (D9): Y_N = N^(1/3)(1 - t^3 - f_N) = C t^2 + D_N - N^(-2/3) Delta1. The leading correction is negative (f_N < 1 - t^3). The drift D_N is positive and falls like N^(-1/3) ln N. BAND_Y = 1/1000 is a lane band chosen by this design, not the owner's: the owner's 1/1000 is the bracket precision target, read only in BEC-T01 and BEC-T02. A MET here does not certify the remainder, which stays OPEN (BEC-T07). Fixed by inputs at the six exposed TS points (XP2). At the four t = 7/10 points no series was evaluated, but the frozen six-term values fix Y_N there to 2.4e-13 or better if the D9 residual pattern holds, at least 8 orders inside BAND_Y, so those reads test the arithmetic and the engines, not the expansion.|points=TS (10 points)|predicted=C t^2 from BEC-K01; D_N = 0.070131835511, 0.054227497682, 0.036995860783, 0.023514798636, 0.123939768303, 0.089277330129, 0.058594811318, 0.036351428686, 0.127732913162, 0.081896800262; the next term alone (t/c3)(ln(t n/c3) + gamma - 19/24)/n = 0.065276426, 0.053010220, 0.036691113, 0.023438558, 0.119076529, 0.088059074, 0.058289941, 0.036275173, 0.126514113, 0.081591862; Y_as = 0.615759537227, 0.599855199398, 0.582623562499, 0.569142500352, 1.193370063666, 1.158707625493, 1.128025106681, 1.105781724049, 1.895566666722, 1.849730553822; f_as = 0.798030057847, 0.837509050038, 0.856793013672, 0.866107148432, 0.507828742042, 0.584580773407, 0.621749215416, 0.639722160562, 0.152527083330, 0.213195920193 (TS order); reads: abs(Y_N - Y_as) <= BAND_Y = 1/1000 and <= 1e-5 (sharp) at all 10; certified f_N^hi < 1 - t^3 at all 10|verdict_rule=READ3 on each read|method=Y bracket from the BEC-T01 f bracket at p = 128 (width far below 1e-20); the reader recomputes D_N with BEC-K01 and BEC-K02 constants|falsifier=any MISS (NOT_MET); PF7 shifts D_N by (t/c3)(19/24)/n, at least 0.0058 (t = 1/2, n = 64), and must read NOT_MET|cost=shared with BEC-T01|prefreeze=COMPUTED: Mellin closed forms at the row points (lane SCALING design.py; this synthesis calc/c7_scaling.py, nums.py); the series at 6 TS points (XP2); the prototype at excluded t = 3/5 matched the six-term Y within 1e-11; final critic k4 (SM8, XP5: Mellin forms at every TS t n, t = 7/10 included); fix-pass f11_t710.py (XP2: the Y_N size at t = 7/10, Mellin forms only); verifier round 1 v6_spot.py (SM10: D_N, Y_as and f_as at (1/2, 8))|from=SC-T03 (owner band relabelled BAND_Y)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T05|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=The leading correction alone does not reach BAND_Y at reachable N. Claim L1: abs(Y_N - C t^2) <= 1/1000. With the drift D_N of BEC-T04 between 0.0235 and 0.128, 23 to 128 times BAND_Y, L1 is designed NOT_MET; it is also NOT_MET with the rounded 2.18 in place of C. The outcome is fixed once BEC-T04's bands hold, so this row is not a negative control. It is not a claim that the owner's law fails: the owner gave the leading term with smaller corrections.|points=TS (10 points)|predicted=MISS (designed NOT_MET) at all 10: Y_N - C t^2 = D_N from 0.0235 (t = 1/2, n = 64) to 0.1277 (t = 9/10, n = 16); Y_N - 2.18 t^2 = D_N + 0.0025108 t^2|verdict_rule=MET if every read is MISS|method=as BEC-T04|falsifier=any read MET or NOT_RESOLVED (a drift 20 times smaller than frozen)|cost=shared|prefreeze=COMPUTED: as BEC-T04|from=SC-T04 (fixed_by_inputs; relabelled)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T06|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=The third Mellin coefficient, from the s = 1 pole. g_N = (Y_N - C t^2 - (5/16) N^(-2/3)) c3 N^(1/3)/t - ln(t N^(1/3)/c3) tends to gamma - 19/24. The read uses the one certified gamma of BEC-K01 and a precision far beyond 1/1000. It tests the expansion one order past the owner's two terms. Fixed by inputs at the six exposed TS points (XP2). At the four t = 7/10 points the frozen values fix g_N to 2.9e-12 or better if the D9 residual pattern holds, far inside the +/- 0.002 band, so those reads test the arithmetic and the engines, not the expansion.|points=TS (10 points)|predicted=gamma - 19/24 in [-0.214451001765133806060154576585, -0.214451001765133806060154576584] (BEC-K01); centres gamma - 19/24 - (19/2880)(c3/t)^2 N^(-2/3) = -0.214917150, -0.214567539, -0.214480136, -0.214458285, -0.214688833, -0.214510460, -0.214465866, -0.214454718, -0.214486970, -0.214459994; band +/- 0.002; resolution at p = 128 below 1e-20; ln(t n/c3) = 1.324949635989, 2.018096816549, 2.711243997109, 3.404391177669, 1.661421872611, 2.354569053171, 3.047716233730, 3.740863414290, 2.605883481451, 3.299030662011 (TS order)|verdict_rule=READ3 on each read|method=reader on the BEC-T04 Y bracket with the certified logarithm|falsifier=any MISS (NOT_MET)|cost=shared|prefreeze=COMPUTED: Mellin closed forms (lane SCALING design2.py; this synthesis nums.py); XP2; final critic k4 (SM8, XP5); fix-pass f11_t710.py (XP2: the g_N size at t = 7/10, Mellin forms only); verifier round 1 v6_spot.py (SM10: the centre and ln(t n/c3) at (1/2, 8))|from=SC-T05 (certified gamma)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T07|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=OPEN|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=The canonical finite-N remainder R_N = Y_N - C t^2 - D_N is not certified (owner: it stays OPEN until certified). BEC-T03 certifies the enclosure of Y_N through the identity and the Chernoff bound, without the Mellin expansion. The Mellin series diverge for every x > 0 (D9), so no convergence radius exists. A proof must bound the contour-shifted Mellin integral at a fixed truncation (past s = -3 for S, s = -2 for V), or bound S - S_M6 directly by Euler-Maclaurin with remainder.|points=TS|predicted=no verdict; OPEN until a proven bound abs(R_N) <= r(x) is frozen in a dated addendum|verdict_rule=none (OPEN)|method=none in this freeze|falsifier=a MISS in BEC-T04 or BEC-T06 refutes the conjectured size of the remainder|cost=none|prefreeze=none|from=SC-T06 (divergence sentence corrected)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T08|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=S|statement=Condensate fluctuations at fixed t (D9): Var(N_0)/N = (zeta(2)/zeta(3)) t^3 + (t^2/c3^2)[(3/2) ln(t N^(1/3)/c3) + (3/2)(1 + gamma) + zeta(2) - 1/4] N^(-1/3) - (t/(2 c3)) N^(-2/3) + (5/96)/N + ... The leading law is REPORTED (BECCITE R1 to R4, verified=0, cited as the owner gave them); everything beyond it is derived here. Fixed by inputs at the six exposed TS points (XP2). At the four t = 7/10 points the frozen values fix Var_N/N to 3.1e-12 (relative) or better if the D9 residual pattern holds, far inside the sharp 1e-5 band, so those reads test the arithmetic and the engines, not the expansion.|points=TS (10 points)|predicted=V_as = Var/N = 0.326372231345, 0.263963358343, 0.224918517495, 0.201635586897, 0.803099735427, 0.665648760056, 0.581909783191, 0.532762127121, 1.339389005638, 1.192176006254 (TS order); leading values as BEC-K01; reads abs(Var_N/(N V_as) - 1) <= 1e-3 and sharp <= 1e-5 at all 10|verdict_rule=READ3 on each read|method=Var bracket by the cancellation-free form (D3) at p = 128 (relative width about 2 W_bound/f + 8 N u, below 1e-24)|falsifier=any MISS (NOT_MET)|cost=O(N) beyond BEC-T01|prefreeze=COMPUTED: Mellin closed forms (lane SCALING design.py; this synthesis nums.py); XP2; the prototype at excluded t = 3/5 matched within 1e-10 relative; final critic k4 (SM8, XP5); fix-pass f11_t710.py (XP2: the Var/N size at t = 7/10, Mellin forms only); verifier round 1 v6_spot.py (SM10: V_as and the BEC-T09 ratio at (1/2, 8))|from=SC-V01|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T09|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=The leading fluctuation law alone is approached slowly. Claim V1: abs(Var_N/((zeta(2)/zeta(3)) t^3 N) - 1) <= 1/10. The N^(-1/3) ln N correction keeps the ratio between 1.135 and 1.91 up to N = 262144, so V1 is designed NOT_MET; fixed once BEC-T08 holds, so not a negative control.|points=TS (10 points)|predicted=MISS (designed NOT_MET) at all 10: V_as/leading = 1.908006, 1.543157, 1.314897, 1.178783, 1.711007, 1.418168, 1.239761, 1.135052, 1.342628, 1.195059 (TS order)|verdict_rule=MET if every read is MISS|method=as BEC-T08|falsifier=any read MET or NOT_RESOLVED|cost=shared|prefreeze=COMPUTED: as BEC-T08|from=SC-V02 (fixed_by_inputs)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T10|kind=CONTRAST|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=1|statement=Canonical against grand canonical at the scaling points. Var_N <= V(q_N) (D4; every TS point has M >= 8) and <N_0> >= N - S(q_N) bound the ratio Var_N/(<N_0>(<N_0>+1)) by closed forms. Claim: the ratio is at most 1/40 at every condensed point; the grand-canonical variance is larger by a factor of 70 to 1e6.|points=TS (10 points); TC read and report|predicted=ratios (TS order) 0.0009985, 9.185e-5, 9.350e-6, 1.025e-6, 0.006059, 0.0004754, 4.594e-5, 4.966e-6, 0.01403, 0.0008003, all <= 1/40; at TC read and report (truncated-Gaussian estimate about 0.46; the Mellin value 3.97 does not apply there)|verdict_rule=MET if the certified upper bound of every ratio is <= 1/40|method=upper Var bracket over the lower <N_0>(<N_0>+1) bracket, in rationals, and the closed-form bound|falsifier=a certified ratio above 1/40 at a condensed point (NOT_MET)|cost=shared|prefreeze=COMPUTED: Mellin values (lane SCALING design.txt; this synthesis nums.py); XP2; the TC estimate recomputed with Delta1 = sigma phi(M)/Phi(M) (fix-pass f1_gauss.py; the earlier 0.8 used the mean of (m - N)+); final critic k4 and k9 (SM8, XP5); verifier round 1 (SM10: v3_gauss.py at TC; v6_spot.py, the ratio at (1/2, 8))|from=SC-V03|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-T11|kind=MODEL_ASYMPTOTIC|tag=CONJECTURE|control=NEGATIVE (the TC read)|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Where the critical region begins (D15). The condensed law needs N - S(q_N) >> sqrt(V) and x (N - S) >> 1. The shifted critical point t_c(N) solves S(q_N(t)) = N on the Mellin form; to first order t_c = 1 - C/(3 N^(1/3)). Rule: rows use only t <= t_M8(N), M = (N - S)/sqrt(V) = 8, with a Chernoff certificate. Control: t = 9/10 is critical at N = 512 but condensed at N = 4096 (M = 8.43) and N = 32768 (M = 35.35). The owner's leading correction is not for the narrow critical region, and this row tests that the window is where predicted.|points=TC against TS (9/10, 16) and (9/10, 32); the rule over all TS|predicted=t_c(N) = 0.830774, 0.909021, 0.953647, 0.976824, 0.988468; t_M6(N) = 0.582536, 0.803350, 0.915180, 0.963342, 0.983766; t_M8(N) = 0.523944, 0.771173, 0.902692, 0.958887, 0.982203 for N = 64, 512, 4096, 32768, 262144; every TS point satisfies t <= t_M8(N); at TC, BAND_Y and the sharp band of BEC-T04 read MISS (designed NOT_MET) with Y_as - Y_N >= 0.02; read and report at TC: Y_as - Y_N (truncated-Gaussian estimate 0.230, from Delta1 = sigma phi(M)/Phi(M) = 14.73 with M = 0.484 and sigma = 28.49), f_N (estimate 0.0557, while f_as = 0.0270), Var_N/(N V_as) (estimate 0.48, unchanged: the variance formula was right); the exact Delta1 was 2.17 times the Gaussian value at the excluded (4/5, 6) and 0.90 to 2.55 times it at the excluded q = 2/3, N = 32 to 56, so these sizes carry no verdict; the 0.02 threshold of the designed MISS holds with a wide margin|verdict_rule=MET if the designed MISS occurs at TC and every TS point satisfies the rule|method=as BEC-T01 and BEC-T04 at TC|falsifier=abs(Y_N - Y_as) < 0.02 at TC (the window is not where predicted), or a TS point above t_M8 (NOT_MET)|cost=shared (N = 512, under 1 s)|prefreeze=COMPUTED: M, t_c, t_M6, t_M8 by bisection on the Mellin forms and the Gaussian estimate (lane SCALING design.py, design2.py; judge-math j6_scaling.py; this synthesis calc/c7_scaling.py, nums.py, all in floats); the Gaussian estimate recomputed with sigma phi(M)/Phi(M) in 60-digit Decimal (fix-pass f1_gauss.py; the earlier 0.131 and 0.0434 used the mean of (m - N)+); the exact near-critical truncation was seen only at excluded q = 2/3 and (t, n) = (4/5, 6), by lane SCALING and again by the fix pass; TC's x was in lane SCALING's calibration (XP2); final critic k4 and k9 (SM8); verifier round 1 (SM10: v3_gauss.py, the Mellin forms and the Gaussian estimate at TC; M and x(N - S) from Mellin forms at (1/2, 8), (9/10, 16), (9/10, 32) and (7/10, 8), in no saved script, XP2)|from=SC-X01 (size reads read and report)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-N01|kind=NUMERICS|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Interval mode is sound where the exact answer is known. At a dyadic q the input has zero width, so each interval engine bounds only its own rounding. Its brackets for Z_N, S_N, T_N, f, Var(N_0) and lambda_1 must contain the exact rationals from the exact engines. q = 3/4 is included up to N = 512 (judge-design).|points=DY (9 points), engines A and B|predicted=every bracket contains its exact value; lo <= hi everywhere; no GUARD rows; the relative width of the Z_N bracket is below 2^-100|verdict_rule=exact rational comparisons with the BEC-X01 values; MET if all hold|method=bec-a interval --q a/b --n N --p 128 and bec_b.py interval|falsifier=an exact value outside its bracket, or lo > hi (NOT_MET); F4 (inward rounding) inverts the bracket from N = 2 at q = 1/2 and must read NOT_MET|cost=under 1 s per point|prefreeze=COMPUTED only at excluded q = 5/8 (lane ENGINE smoke_interval.py: contained at p = 128 and p = 24; inverted under inward rounding)|from=BEC-E06|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-N02|kind=NUMERICS|tag=DERIVED|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=The opposite-endpoint rule, checked from the printed ends (D13). Each interval print carries the raw dyadic ends of Z, S, T, the lambda_1 sum and the cancellation-free Var. The reader recomputes f = [S_lo/(N Z_hi), S_hi/(N Z_lo)] exactly and requires the printed f bracket to contain it; it recomputes the recombined Var bracket [T_lo/Z_hi - (S_hi/Z_lo)^2, T_hi/Z_lo - (S_lo/Z_hi)^2] and requires the printed cancellation-free bracket to intersect it (rule INTERSECT). This is a soundness check only; the scored Var bracket is the cancellation-free one.|points=TS and TC (engine A at 11, engine B at the 9 with N <= 32768); DY; the BEC-T02 reruns|predicted=every containment and intersection holds; lo <= hi everywhere|verdict_rule=exact rational comparisons; MET if all hold|method=reader on the printed dyadic ends|falsifier=a printed f bracket that does not contain the recombination, a disjoint Var pair, or lo > hi (NOT_MET); F5 (same endpoints) must read NOT_MET at (1/2, 512) and (7/10, 512)|cost=under 1 s at the reader|prefreeze=COMPUTED only at excluded t = 5/7 (lane ENGINE smoke_interval.py: the recombination held for the correct rule and failed for the same-endpoint rule at every N)|from=BEC-E07|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-N03|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=The two interval engines agree. Engine A (Z and E recursions, Apery zeta(3), alternating exp) and engine B (E recursion, Amdeberhan-Zeilberger zeta(3), positive exp) certify their own q brackets and run the same frozen interval rules. Where both run, their q, f and Var brackets intersect and their widths are comparable.|points=TS and TC with N <= 32768 (9 points); N = 262144 only if a local engine B run is filed|predicted=all q, f and Var brackets intersect (COMPARE C3, C4); width ratio W_A/W_B in [1/16, 16]; the two N = 262144 points NOT_MEASURED for engine B unless filed (rule STOP)|verdict_rule=rule INTERSECT and READ3 on the width ratio; MET if all hold|method=reader|falsifier=disjoint brackets (at least one engine is wrong) or a width ratio outside [1/16, 16] (MISS)|cost=engine B 19 min per N = 32768 point (3 points), 18 s per N = 4096 point|prefreeze=COMPUTED only at excluded t = 5/7 (lane ENGINE smoke_interval.py: the E bracket met the Z bracket at all 5 N, width ratio 0.97 to 1.04; series_check.py: the engine B series meet the engine A series)|from=BEC-E09|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-N04|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Reproducibility. Exact sums are integer sums, so engine A gives the same bytes on 1 and 4 threads. Interval sums use 64 fixed chunks of k, each summed in order and combined in chunk order, which does not depend on the thread count. Pins: rust-toolchain 1.81.0, Cargo.lock with --locked and no dependencies, Python 3.13.16, this file's sha256 sidecar, and every engine source's sha256 in each receipt's head row. Engine A has no dependency, so it computes those hashes with its own in-crate SHA-256 (src/sha256.rs) over its sources embedded at build time by include_bytes!; a unit test checks that SHA-256 against three FIPS 180-4 vectors: "abc" gives ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad, the empty string gives e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855, and the 448-bit message abcdbcdecdefdefgefghfghighijhijkijkljklmklmnlmnomnopnopq gives 248d6a61d20638b8e5c026930c3e6039a33ce45964ff2167f6ecedd419db06c1; the reader recomputes every source hash with hashlib from the checkout and requires equality. Engine B and the reader print their own sources' hashes by hashlib.|points=CS; TS (1/2, 16)|predicted=cmp equal for 1 against 4 threads at CS and at (1/2, 16); READ-SHORT.hbp regenerated byte for byte in CI and READ-LONG.hbp by the dispatch job; the three SHA-256 vectors pass; every head-row source hash equals the reader's|verdict_rule=MET if every cmp is equal and every hash check holds|method=jobs bec-canonical and bec-canonical-long; cargo test sha256_vectors; tools/read.py hash check|falsifier=any cmp difference, a failed SHA-256 vector, or a head-row hash that differs from the reader's (NOT_MET)|cost=CI short job under 15 min, of which BEC-F01's planted faults take under 10 min|prefreeze=COMPUTED: the three FIPS 180-4 SHA-256 vectors above, checked with hashlib by fix-pass f11_t710.py (FIPS vectors, SM9); no engine quantity|from=BEC-E19 (retagged NUMERICS, CONJECTURE)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-N05|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=-|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=No float and no dependency on the engine path. The gate is sims/bec-canonical/tools/integer_only.py, a copy of ternary/tools/integer_only.py at ac5b158 whose AST and token checks are unchanged; only the two scan-root lists in main() change, to files(["tools", "engine-b"], ".py") and files(["engine-a/src", "engine-a/tests"], ".rs"), relative to sims/bec-canonical (the original's roots, tools/ and src/, tests/, examples/ beside it, would miss engine-a/ and engine-b/ entirely); the docstring is kept, so a CI step can require that the diff against the original is exactly those two lines. On the clean tree its summary line shows python_files=P, rust_files=R, hits=0 and OK, with P >= 6 (tools/read.py, compare.py, audit.py, check_points.py and integer_only.py, and engine-b/bec_b.py) and R >= 11 (engine A's ten src files, sha256.rs included, and at least one file in tests/). Its bans (true division, float and complex literals, float(), round() and complex(), the math, cmath, fractions, decimal, statistics, random and numpy imports, negative literal powers and float format codes) cover engine B and the reader, which use integer-pair rationals. engine-a/Cargo.toml has an empty [dependencies] and Cargo.lock lists one package; engine B imports only sys and hashlib (stdlib); an extra grep for f32 or f64 finds nothing, but F7 does not rely on it.|points=the repository at the run commit|predicted=the gate copy reads hits=0 with python_files >= 6 and rust_files >= 11; the diff is exactly the two root lines; 0 grep hits; one package in Cargo.lock; the only imports in bec_b.py are sys and hashlib; F7 (one planted float literal in each of tools/, engine-b/, engine-a/src/ and engine-a/tests/, in a temporary copy of sims/bec-canonical) is reported by the gate copy as four FAIL lines, one per root, with python_files and rust_files each two above the clean run, and exit 1|verdict_rule=MET if every gate holds and all four F7 literals are reported|method=job bec-canonical gate steps (python3 -I -B tools/integer_only.py; diff against ternary/tools/integer_only.py); tools/planted_faults.sh for F7|falsifier=any hit on the clean tree, a file count below its minimum, a diff other than the two root lines, any extra dependency, or an F7 literal that the gate copy does not report (NOT_MET)|cost=seconds|prefreeze=none|from=BEC-E20 (retagged; reader gate scope stated)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-N06|kind=NUMERICS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=NEGATIVE (PF6)|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Receipt audit for the separate observables and the sequence gates. Frozen keys: K1 a field a0= with any value other than 0; K2 a0_abs2; K3 phase=; K4 coherent, condensate_phase or symmetry_breaking (any case); K5 GP, Gross-Pitaevskii or Bogoliubov as an output quantity (rule GATE_GP); K6 a receipt head row whose features= or plant= field is not empty or none (rule FAULTBUILD). Files scanned: sims/bec-canonical/receipts/*.hbp, READ-SHORT.hbp and READ-LONG.hbp; the README is scanned for K1 to K3 only. READ rows carry only ids, read names and values, never statement text, so the coherent-state verdict of BEC-G02 cannot trip K4 in the clean audit.|points=every receipt; a planted copy|predicted=0 hits in the clean audit; PF6 (a mock receipt line of record BECREAD with qty=a0_abs2 and val=<N_0>) is flagged by K2 (designed NOT_MET of the audit on the planted copy); a planted fault-build receipt (features=fault-f3) is flagged by K6 and refused by the reader|verdict_rule=MET if the clean audit is empty and both planted copies are flagged|method=tools/audit.py with the frozen key list|falsifier=an offending clean line, or a planted copy not flagged (NOT_MET)|cost=seconds|prefreeze=none|from=BC-X18 (audit part), judge-design (frozen keys, fault-build receipts)|json=0
PREDICT|id=BEC-F01|kind=FAULTS|tag=CONJECTURE|control=NEGATIVE|fixed_by_inputs=0|statement=Planted-fault registry. Each fault is built or applied separately, never produces a receipt (rule FAULTBUILD), and must be detected, meaning a NOT_MET of a named row or a GUARD row (rule GUARD), while the clean run stays MET. PF1 = F2: engine B keeps the ground state, weight (1-q^k)^-3 instead of (1-q^k)^-3 - 1. PF2: engine A prints <N_0>(<N_0>+1) as Var. PF3: Boltzmann counting Z_N = Z_1^N/N! in engine A. PF4 = F1a: engine A's recursion sums k = 1..N-1. F1b: Z_1(q^(k+1)) in place of Z_1(q^k) in engine A. F3: degeneracy n+1 instead of (n+1)(n+2)/2, in A, in B, and in both. PF5: engine A's big-by-big multiply (both operands of at least 2 limbs) drops the carry out of limb 1. F4: inward rounding. F5: same-endpoint ratio. F6: one decimal digit flipped in engine A's record of Z at (1/2, 16). F7: a float literal planted in each of the four roots the gate scans, tools/ and engine-b/ (Python) and engine-a/src/ and engine-a/tests/ (Rust), in a temporary copy of sims/bec-canonical. PF6: a mock coherent-state receipt line. PF7: the reader drops -19/24 from S's third term. PF8: engine B's reconstruction is starved or poisoned: (a) --plant fewprimes builds every modulus from half the primes its bound needs, at least one; (b) --plant keepprime skips the test that p divides no c_k, so at q = 1/2 engine B keeps its first prime 2^31 - 1, which divides c_31 = 2^31 - 1. PF9: the reader's truncated-trace routine is fed a coherent state (BEC-O02). T01 (a) and (b) are carried by BEC-T01.|points=CS (q = 1/2, 3/4, N <= 32); DY; TS (1/2, 8), (7/10, 8); reader-only for F6, PF6, PF7, PF9; unit tests for PF5, F3, F4|predicted=PF1: B's Z_1 = 9 against A's 8 at q = 1/2: BEC-X01 (a), (b), (c) and BEC-C01 NOT_MET at N = 1; B's own vector still sums to 1 and its reconstruction checks still pass, since the fault is in the model, not the arithmetic. PF2: BEC-X01 (a) Var and BEC-L01 (equality) NOT_MET at every N. PF3: BEC-C02, BEC-C03 and BEC-X01 NOT_MET from N = 2. PF4: Z_1 = 0, a GUARD positive row at N = 1 (BEC-X02), and BEC-C01 and BEC-X01 NOT_MET at N = 1. F1b: Z_1 = 64/27 against 8 at q = 1/2: BEC-C01, BEC-X01 and BEC-X02 (27 does not divide D_1 = 1) NOT_MET at N = 1. F3: Z_1 = 4, <N_0> = 1/4 against 1/8 at q = 1/2: BEC-C01 and BEC-X02 (Z_1 D_1 = 4 is not divisible by b^3 = 8) NOT_MET and the degeneracy_series unit test fails (1, 2, 3, 4, 5 in place of 1, 3, 6, 10, 15); BEC-X01 NOT_MET when only one engine has it; with both, BEC-X01 is MET and BEC-C01 and BEC-X02 still catch it. PF5: the unit fixture big_mul_allones, (2^(32m) - 1)^2 for m = 2..8 and (2^(32j) - 1)^3 for j = 2..4, differs from the true product (deterministic, scored); run-level expectation, not scored: a GUARD exact_div row (BEC-X02) at some n >= 2 at the first CS point, since D_M is formed by such products; at q = 1/2 and 3/4, c_1 = 1 makes every n = 1 division exact, and k = 2 first divides by c_2^3 = 27 or 343 (the c9 prototype reached n = 1 only because c_1 = 3 at 5/8 and 5 at 2/7). F4: BEC-N01 NOT_MET at q = 1/2, N = 2 and 16 (inverted bracket excluding the exact value; no failure at N = 1, where every step is exact), and the primitive tests fail. F5: BEC-N02 NOT_MET at (1/2, 512) and (7/10, 512) in A and in B. F6: exactly one MISS in BEC-X01 (a). F7: the copied integer_only gate (BEC-N05) reports all four planted literals, one FAIL line per root, and exits 1. PF6: BEC-N06 flags it. PF7: BEC-L05 NOT_MET at all five q (shift 0.864, 1.14, 2.75, 7.51, 78.8) and BEC-T04 NOT_MET. PF8 (a): engine B's reconstruction fails, or fails its extra-prime check, and B prints BECGUARD check=recon from N = 2 at q = 1/2 and 3/4 and at every larger CS point; at N = 2 the frozen BEC-C02 variances need moduli of 41 and 79 bits, and half the bound leaves one 31-bit prime; BEC-X01 NOT_MET there. PF8 (b): every residue mod 2^31 - 1 is wrong from m = 31, so at q = 1/2 the check fails at N = 31 and 32 and BEC-X01 is NOT_MET there, while N <= 30 stay MET. A wrong fraction passes the extra-prime check only with probability about 2^-30, and the reader's byte comparison against engine A catches it anyway. PF9: BEC-O02 reads MISS on the planted copy in all 48 TRUNC runs|verdict_rule=MET if every fault is detected at its named rows and the clean run is MET|method=tools/planted_faults.sh: cargo build --features fault-f1a, fault-f1b, fault-f3, fault-f4, fault-f5, fault-pf2, fault-pf3, fault-pf5; bec_b.py --plant f2, f3, f4, f5, fewprimes, keepprime; the reader's fixtures for F6, PF6, PF7, PF9; temporary copies for F7|falsifier=a planted fault that goes undetected, or a clean row that turns NOT_MET|cost=under 10 min in all (builds and CS runs)|prefreeze=COMPUTED at excluded points only: PF1 to PF4 at 3/5 (SM1); F1a, F1b, F2, F3 at 2/7, 5/8, 3/1000, 47/50 (SM3); F4 and F5 at 5/8 and t = 5/7 (SM3); PF5 at 5/8 and 2/7 (this synthesis calc/c9_pf5_excluded.py: the fixture differs for m >= 2, and the emulated scheme hits GUARD exact_div at n = 1, k = 1 at both q); PF8 at the excluded 5/8 and 2/7 only (fix-pass f7_mm_smoke.py: half the primes failed all 20 fractions at each q; a kept prime dividing c_28 or c_40 failed exactly the fractions at N >= 28 or N >= 40, and no wrong fraction passed); the PF8 (a) sizes at N = 2 read from the frozen BEC-C02 strings (XP4); F6, F7, PF6, PF9 none; verifier round 1 (SM10: v5_multimod.py, PF8 at the excluded 2/7 and 5/8 and the N = 2, 3 needs from the frozen BEC-C02 and C03 strings; v6_spot.py, the F1b, F3 and PF1 values at q = 1/2); the final critic k6 (SM8: the fault values)|from=BC-X21 (PF5 redefined so it must fire), BEC-E13 (flip list completed), BEC-E14, BEC-E15, BEC-E16, BEC-E17, BEC-E18|json=0
